        "title": "EXAMPLE 11.7",
        "problem": "EXAMPLE 11.7\nDielectric\nPolarization of a dielectric in an electric field gives rise to thin layers of bound charges on the surfaces, creating positive and negative surface charge densities.\nFigure shows a different combination of capacitors, if the total charge is 600μC. Then determine the values of V, and Cz.\nPHYSICS-XII\nNOT FOR SALE\n40\nUNIT 11 ELECTROSTATICS\nGIVEN\ntotal charge Q- 600μC, capacitance C,-15 μF,\ncapacitance C,= 8uF, Potential V2= 20V\nC, 15μF\nC, 8uF\nV1 20V\nCapacitors C1, C2, & C, connected to potential V\nREQUIRED\nSOLUTION\ncapacitance C2-?, Potential V1=?\nP.D. across capacitor C,: V-600x10 C 15x10+ Total P.D.: V=V,+V12 =40+20=60V\nCharge on capacitor C, is :Q,=C, XV2\n40V\naze in\n=(8×10*)x20\n=160x10°C=160μC\nCharge on capacitor C, is: Q =600-160-440μC\n.. Capacitance of capacitor C2-\n440 x10\n20\n=22×10*F=22μF",
