        "theory": "the current through the galvanometer is\nA. 1 A\nB. O A C. Maximum\nD. Half of the maximum value\nCONCEPTUAL QUESTIONS\nж\nA heavy duty battery of a truck maintains a current of 3A for 24 hour. How much charge flows from the battery during this time?\n2 While analysing a circuit the internal resistance of e.m.f. sources are\nignored why?\nPHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 12 CURRENT ELECTRICITY\nNOT FOR SALE\n85\n3 If aluminum and copper wires of the same length have the same\nresistance, which has the larger diameter? Why?\nUnder what circumstances can the terminal P.D. of a battery exceed its e.m.f.?\n5 What is the difference between an e.m.f. and a P.D.?\n6 How the loop rule and junction rule are based on the conservation of\nenergy principle?\n7 Why rise in temperature of a conductor is accompanied by a rise in the\nresistance?\nDoes the direction of e.m.f. provided by a battery depend on the direction of current flow through the battery?\nVoltages are always measured between two points. Why?\nIs every emf a potential difference? Is every potential difference an emf?\nHow much charge flow in pocket calculator each minute when the current is 0.0001A?\n2 When Wheatstone Bridge is balanced, then no current flows through the\ngalvanometer, why?\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTIONS\nDescribe the concept of steady state current as a flow of positive negative or both. Define the unit of current.\nExplain the electronic current in a metallic wire as due to the drift of free electrons in the wire.\nState Ohms law. Discuss its scope and validity (a) discuss resistivity and conductivity of a material (b) how does resistance change with temperature?\nExplain the term: emf, internal resistance and terminal potential difference of a battery.\n5 Explain the construction of rheostat. How is it used as a, (a) control the\ncurrent, (b) as a potential divider?\nWhat is wheat stone bridge? Explain with diagram the balancing, the principle and the working of this bridge?\nWhat is a potentiometer? Explain its principle, construction, and working. What is the advantage of using potentiometer for measuring potential difference?\nPHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 12 CURRENT ELECTRICITY\nNOT FOR SALE\n86\nWhat is thermocouple? Explain the working of thermocouple by drawing its diagram. By sketching curve explain the variation in thermoelectric e.m.f. with Temperature.\nWhy we use Kirchoff&#x27;s law for circuit problems solution. Explain its rules for circuit solution by giving proper example.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEMS\n1 A battery has an e.m.f. of 12.8V and supplies a current of 3.2A. What is the resistance of the circuit? How many coulombs leave the battery in 5minutes?\nAnswer (40, 1200 C)\n2 Two light bulbs designed for 120-V use are rated at 40W and 60W.\nWhich light bulb has the greater filament resistance? Why?\nAnswer (240 0,3600) 3 A carbon electrode has a resistance of 0.1250 at 20 C°. The temperature co-efficient of carbon is -0.0005 at 20C°. What will be the resistance of the electrode at 85 C°?\nAnswer (0.120)\n4 Calculate the resistance of wire 10 m long that has a diameter of 2mm\nand resistivity of 2.63×100 m.\nAnswer (0.0838 0)\n5 A typical 12V automobile battery has a resistance of 0.012 0. What is the terminal voltage of this battery when the starter draws a current of 100A? calculate the R,P, PR and Pr.\nAnswer (10.8 V, 0.108 0, 1200W, 120 W)\n6A 10 watt resister has a value of 120 0. What is the rated current\nthrough the resister?\nAnswer (0.2886 A)\n7 A resistor of 500 has a P. D. of 100V, D.C. across 1 hour. Calculate\n(a). Power and (b). Energy.\nAnswer ((a) 200W, (b) 0.72 MJ)\nCalculate the current through a single loop circuit if £= 120V,\nB\nR = 1000 and internal resistance r = 0.01 0.\nPHYSICS-XII\nAnswer (120 mA)\nn\nUNIT 12. CURRENT ELECTRICITY\n9\nNOT FOR SALE\n87\nFind the terminal potential difference of each cell in circuit of figure.\n80\nwww\nAnswer (23.8 V, 7.8 V)\nx\n10\n0.10-\n24V\n0.90\n6V",
