      "The continuous flow of free electrons is called steady current. The flow of electronic current can be easily explained by referring Figure 12.1. The conductor has a large number of free electrons when electric field or voltage is applied, then free electrons, being negatively charged, will start moving towards the positives terminal around the circuit.",
