        "theory": "2\nBy applying Right hand rule II or Fleming&#x27;s left Hand rule it can be seen that the forces on sides 2 and 4 (F, and F,) are such that they produce a net torque.\nPHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 13 ELECTROMAGNETISM\nIf we view the loop from side 3 and sight along sides 2 and 4, we see the view shown in Figure 13.23. The two magnetic forces F, and F., that the two forces point in opposite directions such that they form a couple. If the loop is pivoted so that it can rotate about point 0, these two forces produce a torque that rotates the loop (in this case clockwise). The magnitude of this torque is\nNOT FOR SALE 110\nFIGURE 13.23\n20\n0\nH-b/2-H\nSide view of a coil in a magnetic field\nputting values of F, and F, from equation 2 in equation 3, we get\nb\nb\nt = IBa=+lBa\nor\nΤ\nt = 2/Ba\n2\nTherefore t = IBab\nSince a is the length and b is the width of the coil, therefore\nab = A\n5\nputting equation 5 in equation 4, we get\nt = IBA\n13.11\nחו\nEquation 13.11 represents the maximum condition for torque on a current carrying loop of wire.\nNow suppose the uniform magnetic field B makes an FIGURE 13.24\nangle 8 &lt; 90&#x27; with a line perpendicular to the plane\nof the loop as in Figure 13.24.\nThe torque is given by relation\nt = IBAsine\n13.12\nF2\nकाल\n14\n2\ne\nB\n42\n-sine\nPHYSICS-XII\nTorque at an angle &lt; 90°\nUNIT 13 ELECTROMAGNETISM\nEXAMPLE 13.5\nNOT FOR SALE\n111\nTORQUE ON A LOOP\nA square loop of wire of side 4.0 cm carries 3.0A of current. A uniform magnetic field of magnitude 0.67 T makes an angle of 30° with the plane of the loop. (a) What is the magnitude of the torque on the loop? (b) What is the net magnetic force on the loop?\nGIVEN\nFor single square loop number of turns &#x27;N&#x27; = 1\nREQUIRED\nMagnetic field &#x27;B&#x27; = 0.6 T\nTorque &#x27;t&#x27; = ?\nArea &quot;A&quot;= ab = 4.0 cm x 4.0 cm = 0.0016 m\nMagnetic force &#x27;F,&quot; = ?\nCurrent &#x27;I&#x27; = 3.0 A\nT\nAngle with plane of the loop p = 30°\nSOLUTION\nThe angle &#x27;0&#x27; between vector area &#x27;A&#x27; and magnetic field &#x27;B&#x27; is 0-90-0-90° - 30° 60°\n(a) The torque on current carrying coil is\nT = NIAB sine\nputting values\nB = 0.6 T\n0 = 60&quot;\n-30&quot;\n20\n1x(3.00 A) x0.0016 mx 0.67sin60°\nHence 2.5x10 Nm\nAnswer\n(b) B sine is the same at opposite sides of the loop and opposite sides of the loop have equal and opposite so the forces on opposite sides are equal and opposite. And net force is zero\nFnet = Ftop +Fbottom +Fright +Fleft\nTherefore Fnet = Flop -Ftop +Fright-Fright\nHence\nFret =ON\nAnswer\n&quot;PHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 13 ELECTROMAGNETISM",
