        "title": "Textbook lesson extract 14",
        "theory": "10 Two parallel wire 10 cm apart carry currents in opposite directions of 8 A.\nWhat is the magnetic field halfway between them?\nPHYSICS-XII\n(Answer: 6.4x10T)\nE\nS\nNOT FOR SALE\n126\nUnit\n14\nELECTROMAGNETIC INDUCTION\nHow electromagnetism works in a metal detector?\nAfter studying this Unit students will be able to:\nA⚫ describe the production of electricity by magnetism.\nLEARNING\naz e\n⚫ explain that induced e.m.f.&#x27;s can be generated in two ways. by relative movement (the generator effect).\n(1)\n(ii)\nby changing a magnetic field (the transformer effect).\ninfer the factors affecting the magnitude of the induced e.m.f.\nstate Faraday&#x27;s law of electromagnetic induction.\naccount for Lenz&#x27;s law to predict the direction of an induced current and relate to the principle of conservation of energy.\napply Faraday&#x27;s law of electromagnetic induction and Lenz&#x27;s law to solve problems.\nPHYSICS-XII\nLEARNING\n5",
        "content": "10 Two parallel wire 10 cm apart carry currents in opposite directions of 8 A.<br>What is the magnetic field halfway between them?<br>PHYSICS-XII<br>(Answer: 6.4x10T)<br>E<br>S<br>NOT FOR SALE<br>126<br>Unit<br>14<br>ELECTROMAGNETIC INDUCTION<br>How electromagnetism works in a metal detector?<br>After studying this Unit students will be able to:<br>A⚫ describe the production of electricity by magnetism.<br>LEARNING<br>az e<br>⚫ explain that induced e.m.f.&#x27;s can be generated in two ways. by relative movement (the generator effect).<br>(1)<br>(ii)<br>by changing a magnetic field (the transformer effect).<br>infer the factors affecting the magnitude of the induced e.m.f.<br>state Faraday&#x27;s law of electromagnetic induction.<br>account for Lenz&#x27;s law to predict the direction of an induced current and relate to the principle of conservation of energy.<br>apply Faraday&#x27;s law of electromagnetic induction and Lenz&#x27;s law to solve problems.<br>PHYSICS-XII<br>LEARNING<br>5",
        "rules": [],
        "sciNote": "10 Two parallel wire 10 cm apart carry currents in opposite directions of 8 A.\nWhat is the magnetic field halfway between them?\nPHYSICS-XII\n(Answer: 6.4x10T)\nE\nS\nNOT FOR SALE\n126\nUnit\n14\nELECTROMAGNETIC INDUCTION\nHow electromagnetism works in a metal detector?\nAfter studying this Unit students will be able to:\nA⚫ describe the production of electricity by magnetism.\nLEARNING\naz e\n⚫ explain that induced e.m.f.'s can be generated in two ways. by relative movement (the generator effect).\n(1)\n(ii)\nby changing a magnetic field (the transformer effect).\ninfer the factors affecting the magnitude of the induced e.m.f.\nstate Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction.\naccount for Lenz's law to predict the direction of an induced current and relate to the principle of conservation of energy.\napply Faraday's law of electromagnetic induction and Lenz's law to solve problems.\nPHYSICS-XII\nLEARNING\n5"
