        "theory": "POINTS\nPHYSICS-XII\nIT 14 ELECTROMAGNETIC INDUCTION\nNOT FOR SALE\n152\nEXERCISE\nChoose the best possible answer\nFor inducing e.m.f. in a coil the basic requirement is that\n(A) Flux should link the coil\n(B) change in flux should link the coil\n(C) coil should form a closed loop\n(D) both (B) and (C) are true\nWhen a single turn coil rotates in a uniform magnetic field, at uniform speed the induced e.m.f. will be\nA. Alternating\nC) Pulsating\n3 Principle of dynamically induced e.m.f. is used in a\n(5)\nA. Choke\nC. Generator\nB)Steady\nB) Transformer\nD) Thermo-couple\nD) zero\nIn Fleming&#x27;s left-hand rule thumb always represents direction of\nA) Current flow\nC) Magnetic field\nB) Induced\ne.m.f.\nD. Mechanical force\nThe field at any point on the axis of a current carrying coil will be A) Perpendicular to the axis.\nC) At an angle of 45° with the axis.\nB. Parallel to the axis. D) Zero.\nWhen a coil rotated in magnetic field the induced current in it\nA. continuously changes\nC. becomes zero\n7\nA.\nB. remains same\nD. becomes maximum\nWazir\nIn A.C generator increasing the number of turns in the coil\ndecreases the Electromotive force (e.m.f.)\nB.\nنة\nelectromotive force (e.m.f.) remains same\nC. increases the Electromotive force (e.m.f.)\n0\nN\nD.\nS\nelectromotive force (e.m.f.) becomes zero\n8 The device in which induced e.m.f. is statically induced e.m.f.is\n(A) transformer\n(C) alternator\n(B) AC generator\n(D) dynamo.\nWhat is the coefficient of mutual inductance, when the magnetic flux changes by 2×102 Wb, and change in current is 0.01 A?\n(A) 2 H\n(B) 3H\nPHYSICS-XII\n(C) 1/2 H\n(D) zero\nUNIT 14 ELECTROMAGNETIC INDUCTION\nNOT FOR SALE\n153\nM 10 The induced e.m.f. in a coil is proportional to\n(A) magnetic flux through the coil\n(B) rate of change of magnetic flux through the coil (C) area of the coil\n(D) product of magnetic flux and area of the coil\nPIn a coil current change from 2 to 4 A in 0.05 s. If the average\ninduced e.m.f. is 8V then coefficient of self-inductance is\nMULTIPLE CHO-CE\n(A) 0.2 henry (B) 0.1 henry (C) 0.8 henry\n(D) 0.04 henry\nWhich of the following quantities remain constant in step\nup transformer?\n(A) current (B) voltage (C) power (D) heat\n13 Step-up transformer has a transformation ratio of 3:2. What is\nthe voltage in secondary, if voltage in primary is 30 V?\n(A) 45 V",
