      "(a): AC waveform for one cycle",
      "CYCLE. One complete set of positive and negative values of an alternating quantity is known as a cycle. Fig. 15.3 (a) shows one cycle of an alternating voltage. A cycle can also be defined in terms of angular measure. One cycle corresponds to 360° or 2m radians.",
      "TIME PERIOD. The time taken in seconds to complete one cycle of an alternating quantity is called its time period. It is generally represented by T.",
      "FREQUENCY. The number of cycle that occurs in one second is called the frequency (ƒ) of the alternating quantity. It is measured in cycle per second or Hertz (Hz). The frequency of power system in Pakistan is 50 Hz. It means that alternating voltage or current completes 50 cycles in",
