      "15.5 PHASE OF A.C. Every alternating wave has a positive half cycle and a negative half cycle in its complete cycle of revolution, along with the coordinate axis. This wave is continues. Consider alternating voltage wave of time period T second as shown in Fig.15.5.The maximum positive value (+1m) occurs at T/4 second or 90°. Therefore phase of maximum positive value is T/4 second or 90°. Similarly, the phase of negative peak (-1) is 37/4 second or 270°.",
      "Alternating voltage wave form",
      "in",
      "So Phase of a particular amplitude of an alternating quantity is the fractional part of time period or cycle through which the quantity has progressed from the selected zero position of reference. The word \"phasor\" is short for \"phase vector.\" It is a way to represent a sine or cosine function graphically. The sinusoidal voltage wave can be represented by a phasor rotating in anticlockwise, at an angular velocity w rad/s about point O. The length of the phasor OA represents the magnitude of (on a suitable scale) of the alternating quantity. The phase of the waveform for one complete revolution is 2m or 360°. Let the line OA representing phasor to be rotating in anticlockwise direction at an angular velocity w rad/s about the point O. If we take the projection of the phasor OA on Y-axis, we get the instantaneous value of the sinusoidal wave",
