      "From Eqs (i) and (iv) it is clear that current lags behind the voltage by π/2 radians or 90°. Hence in a pure inductance, current lags behind the voltage by 90°. Fig. 15.10(b) also shows that current lags the voltage in an inductive coil. Inductance opposes the change in current and serves to delay the increase or",
