      "From Eq. (15.33), it is clear that on increasing either the inductance or the capacitance causes the resonant frequency to decrease. For a given value of inductance and capacitance, there is only one resonant frequency at resonant frequency the current is maximum and impedance of circuit is minimum. Z-R The magnitude of the current as a function of frequency is plotted as resonance curve Fig 15.19 which shows that the current I starts at near to zero, reaches maximum value at the resonance frequency f, and then drops again to nearly zero as ƒ becomes infinite.",
