      "15.14 PRINCIPLE OF METAL DETECTORS",
      "A coil and capacitor are electrical components, which together can produce oscillations of current. An L-C circuit behaves just like an oscillating mass-spring system. In this case, energy oscillates between a capacitor and an inductor. The circuit is called an electrical oscillator. Two such oscillators A and B are used for the operation of common type of metal detector (Fig 15.20). In the absence of any nearby metal object, the inductances L, and La",
