      "The space lattice is a skeleton upon which crystal structure is built by placing atoms on or near the lattice points. Therefore, the study of crystal structure becomes simpler when it is represented by a space lattice. The points which are forming a lattice are called lattice sites. The distance between the consecutive neighbours sites is called lattice constant. When we assign direction to these lattice constant, they become lattice translation vectors. vers lensmith",
