        "theory": "UNIT 17 ELECTRONICS\nNOT FOR SALE\n253\n2 Explain the significance of depletion layer in an equilibrium state in a PN-\njunction. Give energy band diagram.\nExplain how PN-junction acts as a half-wave rectifier.\n4 Explain the working of transistor as an amplifier?\n6 Draw the circuit for a half wave rectifier and full wave rectifier.\n6 Compare the advantages and disadvantages of full wave rectifier and half\nwave rectifier.\nDeduce the relation between a and ẞ of a transistor.\n8 Discuss the conductivity of extrinsic semiconductor and its band gap\nenergy.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEMS\nIn a certain circuit, the transistor has a collector current of 10 mA and a base current of 40 μA. What is the current gain of the transistor?\nAnswer (250)\n2 The current flowing into the base of a transistor is 100 μA. Find its collector current /c, its emitter current lg, and the ratio c/le if the value of current gain ẞ is 100.\nAnswer(10 mA, 10.1mA, 0.99)\n3 A transistor is connected in CE configuration. The voltage drop across the load resistance (Rc) 3 k is 6 V. Find the base current. The current gain a\nof the transistor is 0.97.\nAnswer (2.06×10 A)\nIn a common base circuit, the current gain is 0.96. If the collector current is 60 μ A. Find the emitter current.\nAnswer (62.5 PA)\n5 In transistor, the emitter current (I) is 3.5 A and collector current (c) is\n2.35 A find the base current.\nAnswer ( 1.15 A)\nPHYSICS-XII\nNOT FOR SALE\n254\nUnit\n18\nDAWN OF THE MODERN PHYSICS Tardigrade (water bear) only grow up to 1.5 mm. How are such high resolution images possible for such small creatures?\nLEARN\nN\nAfter studying this unit the students will be able to\ndistinguish between in ertial and non-inertial frames of reference. describe the significance of Einstein&#x27;s assumption of the constancy of the speed of\nlight.\nWa\nidentify that if c is constant then space and time become relative. explain qualitatively ai nd quantitatively the consequence of special relativity in relation to:\nthe relativity of simultaneity\nthe equivalence between mass and energy\n⚫ length contraction\n⚫ time dilation\n• mass increase\nexplain the implications of mass increase, time dilation and length\ncontraction for space : travel.\nPHYSICS-XII",
