      "17.4.1 IV CHARACTERISTICS OF PN JUNCTION",
      "239",
      "The IV characteristics of PN junction are shown in Fig 17.10. The knee volta ge is 0.3V for germanium and 0.7V for silicon junction.From the IV characteristics, we see that the forward current increases rapidly beyond the knee voltage. There exists a maximum current limit for junction, which is decided by power ratio of the junction. Beyond that, the junction is destroyed.",
      "In reverse bias, if voltage is increased, due to available energy, covalent bonds break and large number of electrons are released. This causes a sudden increase in current. This is called as zener effect.",
