      "Heinrich Hertz in 1887, and Einstein FIGURE 18.10",
      "explained it with photon concept of light in 1905. Let us analyze two basic photoelectric experiments, each using the apparatus shown in figure 18.10, in which light of frequency 'f' is directed onto metallic emitter and ejects electrons from it. A potential difference 'V' is maintained between metallic emitter and collector. This arrangement produces a photoelectric current 'I' that is measured with sensitive ammeter \"A\".",
