      "18.8 PAIR PRODUCTION",
      "The creation of an elementary particle and its antiparticle, usually when a photon (or another neutral boson) interacts with a nucleus an electron and its antiparticle, the positron, may be created is called pair production.",
      "y →e*+e ̄",
      "Pair production is the process in which a photon is converted into matter in accordance with Einstein equation E = mc2. A photon when passes near a nucleus it disintegrates into electron and positron pair as shown in figure 18.18. Positron has the same mass as electron but opposite charge.",
