      "Asimilar demonstration of the wave nature of relativistic electrons was provided in the same year by G. P. Thomson, who observed the transmission of electrons with energies in the range of 10 to 40 keV through thin metallic foils (G. P. Thomson, the son of J. J. Thomson, shared the Nobel Prize in Physics in 1937 with Davisson). The wave properties of particles like protons, neutrons, other atoms and even molecules has also been observed. In all cases the measured wavelengths agree with de Broglie's prediction, proving that all matter has wavelike as well as particle like properties.",
