      "319",
      "An electron may lose all or a part of its energy in such a collision. Since different",
      "NOT FOR SALE electrons are slowed down differently in target and thus varying amounts of energies are lost by the electrons in the form of X-rays. Therefore the spectrum obtained is continuous X-ray spectrum. The shortest-wavelength X-ray (the highest frequency) must be due to an electron that gives up all its kinetic energy to produce one photon in a single collision. Since the initial kinetic energy of an electron is equal to the energy given it by the accelerating voltage, V, then",
      "KE = q,V",
