      "therefore q2,V=h",
      "The equation 19.9 agrees with experimentally observed values. This result is further evidence that X-rays are a form of electromagnetic radiation (light) and that the photon theory of light is valid.",
      "E. APPLICATIONS OF X-RAYS",
      "The important practical applications of X-rays can be divided into three categories A. Scientific Applications: The diffraction pattern of X-rays by different. crystals give information about internal structure of crystals. The spacing and dispositions of the atoms of crystals can be determined.",
      "B. Industrial Applications: X-rays penetrating ability can be used to detect defects in Rial roads, bridges and large machinery. The structure of rubber and plastics can be analyzed. It is also used at airports to check customers and baggage and by art historians to see if a picture has been painted on top of an older one. C. Medical Applications: Since bore is more opaque to X-rays than flesh, therefore if X-rays are allowed to pass through the human body a shadow of bone can be obtained on photographic film. The X-ray film reveal the fractures of bones",
      "presence of foreign bodies.",
      "and",
      "PHYSICS-XII",
      "UNIT 19 ATOMIC SPECTRA",
      "NOT FOR SALE",
      "320",
      "High energetic X-rays can be used for therapeutic purposes as well.",
      "For your information",
      "CT SCANNER",
      "The acronym CAT stands for Computerized Axial Tomography or in short CT (Computerized Tomography).",
      "In CT scan machine there are large number of X-ray detectors. The source and detectors are arranged on a large ring shape structure. In this technique a number of X-ray beams pass simultaneously through the patient. The source and detector are rotated to get. views from different directions. Large number of images are obtained and are combined by a computer to get detailed 3D images of the patient. In effect, the CAT scanning technique makes it possible to take an X-ray picture of a cross-sectional 'slice' that is perpendicular to the body's long axis.",
      "EXAMPLE 19.2",
