        "theory": "________PHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 20 NUCLEAR PHYSICS-\nNOT FOR SALE\n367\nAbsorption of a neutron by uranium-238 followed by two beta-decay reactions produces plutonium-239, which can also be used as a fission fuel. Fission can be generated in plutonium-239 by fast neutrons therefore no moderator is required in these reactors. The core of fast reactor consists of mixture of plutonium and uranium dioxide surrounded by U blanket. Thus any neutron escaping from the core interact with &quot;U to produce &quot;Pu. Thus natural uranium is used to generate more nuclear fuel by the reaction as shown in the figure 20.19. 20.14 NUCLEAR FUSION\nWhen two light nuclei combine to form a heavy nucleus, the process is called nuclear fusion. When two nuclei form a large nucleus the mass of larger nucleus is less than the mass of nuclei that formed it. This loss in mass appears in the form of A self sustaining fusion reaction is also possible but the energy required is possible only in the environments of stars including sun. This cycle of reactions can be achieved at stars in two series of processes.\nenergy.\nA. PROTON CYCLE\nIn this process the direct collision of protons result in the formation of heavier nuclei whose collision in tern produces helium nuclei as shown in figure 20.20. The initial reaction in proton-proton cycle is\nFIGURE 20.20\nProton\nProton\nB+\nProton\nProton\nProton\nProtan O\nNeutron\nB+\nH+H\nNeutron\nлий\nm\nH+B++v\nHe\nM\nin\nProton\nProton\nHe\nзне\nHe\nThe proton-proton chain\nPHYSICS-XII\nUNIT 20 NUCLEAR PHYSICS\nNOT FOR SALE\n368\nA deuteron produced in the above reaction may combine with other proton as\nH+ H→ He+y\nFinally, two such reactions can combine to form helium-4 with the release of two protons as\nHe+ He→ He+ H + H+7\nThe total energy released in this process is 24.7 MeV which is the difference between the masses of 4 protons and mass of alpha particle plus two positrons.\nReaction\nEnergy released\nstep 1\nH+H→ H+ B*+v (twice)\n0.42 MeV (twice)\nstep 2\nHe+ He→ He+y (twice)\n5.49 MeV (twice)\nstep 3\nstep 4\nHe+ He→He+ H+H+y\n→\n&gt;Total\nB+B 2y (twice)\n194H→ He+2°B+2v+7y\nB. CARBON CYCLE\nThe carbon cycle proceeds as shown in figure 20.21.\nFIGURE 20.21\n12C\nY\nwww.\n13N\nB+\n12.85 MeV\n1.02 MeV (twice)\n26.71 MeV\nwaze in\nProton\n13C\n1H\nProton &quot;H\nThe carbon-nitrogen chain\nwww\n14N\n150\n1H\n4主\nProton",
