        "theory": "Disgorge: taken out from the throat what has been eaten. Dynamo: from the Greek word dynamis, which means power.\nDynamoelectric: relating to the conversion by induction of mechanical energy into electrical energy or vice versa.\nExtra-terrestrial sources: sources that are existing or originating outside the limits of the earth.\nElectromagnets: a device consisting of a core of magnetic material surrounded by a coil that create a magnetic field through the application of electricity. Electromagnetic Induction: the creation of e.m.f. due to relative motion conductor and magnet.\nElectroplaque: these are cells used by electric eels, and other fish for electrogenesis.\nFrequency: the number of cycles in one second of alternating current. Generator: a device that changes mechanical energy into electrical energy. Insulators: materials that don&#x27;t readily give up electrons, thereby restricting\nthe flow of current.\nPeak inverse voltage (PIV): the maximum voltage V, the diode can withstand during reverse bias is known as peak inverse voltage (PIV).\nNOT FOR SALE 384\nMyelin: a white tissue forming an insulating sheath (myelin sheath) around certainnerve fibres. Damage to the myelin sheath causes neurological disease, as in multiple sclerosis.\nMotor: a device that changes electrical energy into mechanical energy.\nMuon: a negatively charged subatomic particle, with the same charge as an electron.\nOhm: unit of resistance.\nOhm&#x27;s Law: current is directly proportional to voltage and inversely\nproportional to resistance.\nPermanent Magnets: it retain their magnetism after a magnetizing force is removed.\nResistance: the restriction to the flow of electrons.\nRMS Value: Root Mean Square Current is also referred to as effective current and is the square root of the average of all the instantaneous currents. Single-Phase: a continuous single alternating current cycle.\nSpectrum: spectrum means set of frequencies absorbed or emitted by a substance.\nTerrestrial sources: sources that are existing or originating inside the limits of the earth.\nThree-Phase: a continuous series of three overlapping AC cycles offset by 120 degrees.\nTransformer: a device used to raise (step up) or lower (step down) a voltage level.\nVentricle: a chamber of the heart that receives blood from an atrium and pumps it to the arteries.\nVoltage Drop: voltage value as measured across each resistor or load. Voltmeter: a device to measure voltage.\ne inc\nWaveform: the shape of the curve obtained by plotting the instantaneous values of voltage or current as ordinate against time as abscissa is called its\nwaveform or wave shape.\nWatt: the basic unit of power, indicating the amount of work accomplished when one volt causes one ampere to pass through a circuit.\nAuthors Profile\nShaukat Ali Taran did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1988. He also did Master in Education. He is the author and editor of many books of physics.\nCollege, Kohat. Currently, he is working as a Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Timergara (Dir Lower).\nShadab Gul did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1996. He taught various classes for more than 20 years at school as well as college level. Currently he is working as Assistant Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Lakki\nMarwat.\nAbdul Baseer did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1990. Currently he is working as a professor in Edwardes College, Peshawer.\nAbdur-Rehman did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 2008. He taught Physics in various private and govt institutions. Currently he is working as a Lecturer in Durrani School and College, Peshawer.\nDr. Muhammad Naeem Khalid remained Chairman of Physics Department, Islamia College, Peshawer.\nAamir Ullah Khan has obtained MS - Physics and is currently working as &#x27;Director&quot; at Pakistan Virtual College, Hayatabad Peshawar.\nHe is the co-author of general science textbooks for grade 6, grade 7 and grade 8 under the National Book Foundation. He is also the co-author of physics textbooks for grade 9, grade 10 and grade 11 of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board,\nPeshawar.\nHafiz Mehar Elahi did MS/M.Phil Physics from Qurtuba University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar. Recently honoured with Best Chaperone Award by GIK Institute of Sciences and Information Technology. He got First position ir BS-Physics from Govt College Peshawar in 2014 affiliated with UOP.Currently he working as Lecturer in Physics at Peshawar Model Degree, College.\nKhyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board\nPhase - V, Hayatabad Peshawar\nPhone: 091-9217714-15 Fax: 091-9217163, Website: www.kptbb.gov.pk\nTEXTBOOK FEEDBACK FORM\nS#\nStatement\n1.\nOverall the book is interesting and user friendly.\n2.\nThe language and content of the book is age / grade appropriate and the content is free of grammatical and punctuation errors.\n3. Content is supported with examples from real life/culture.\n4.\nContents / texts are authentic and updated.\n5.\nPictures / diagrams/graphs / illustrations are informative,\n6.\nrelevant and clear if not, then identify them.\nActivities, projects and additional work is suggested for\nreinforcement of concepts.\n7.\nAssessment achievements are thought provoking and\nRemarks\n8.\ncomprise cognitive, psychomotor and effective skills.\nThe textbook is easy to be covered within academic year.\nPage No.\nGeneral Remarks:\nObservation/comments\nName &amp; Address:\nContact No. &amp; Email:\nSuggested amendment along with rationale\nائی بھائی ہیں۔\nمیں صلح کرا دیا کرو و تاکہ تم پر رحمت\n(سورة الحجرات: ۱۰)\nZ\nپاکیزہ چیزوں میں تم کو دی ہیں۔\n(سورۃ البقرہ: آیت ۱۷۲)\nمومن تو آپس میں ؟ پس اپنے دو بھائیوں\nاور اللہ سے ڈرتے ر\nجائے۔",
