      "Absorption of a neutron by uranium-238 followed by two beta-decay reactions produces plutonium-239, which can also be used as a fission fuel. Fission can be generated in plutonium-239 by fast neutrons therefore no moderator is required in these reactors. The core of fast reactor consists of mixture of plutonium and uranium dioxide surrounded by U blanket. Thus any neutron escaping from the core interact with \"U to produce \"Pu. Thus natural uranium is used to generate more nuclear fuel by the reaction as shown in the figure 20.19. 20.14 NUCLEAR FUSION",
