      "20.19 BUILDING BLOCKS OF MATTER",
      "Beginning in about 1945, many new particles were discovered in experiments involving high-energy collisions between known particles. Such particles are highly unstable and have very short half-lives, ranging between 10 and 10\" s. So far, more than 400 of these unstable, temporary particles have been catalogued. It is useful to group the known particles into three families-the bosons, the leptons, and the hadrons.",
      "OSONS",
      "The boson family is composed of particles that play central roles in nature's fundamental forces. The photon is associated with the electromagnetic force. The W, W', and Z' particles are associated with the weak nuclear force. The gluons are associated with the strong nuclear force, whereas the graviton is thought to be",
      "associated with the gravitational force.",
