    "content": "<p>Each second \\(10^{18}\\) electrons flow from right to left across a cross-section of a wire attached to the two terminals of a battery. (a) Calculate the current in the wire. (b) In which direction is the current flowing?</p><p>GIVEN</p><p>\\(n=10^{18}\\); charge on one electron \\(e=1.6\\times10^{-19}\\,\\mathrm C\\); \\(t=1\\,\\mathrm s\\)</p><p>REQUIRED</p><p>(a) Electric current \\(I=?\\); (b) direction of current flow = ?</p><p>SOLUTION</p><p>\\(I=\\frac Qt=\\frac{ne}{t}\\)</p><p>\\(I=\\frac{10^{18}\\times1.6\\times10^{-19}}{1}=1.6\\times10^{-1}\\,\\mathrm A=160\\,\\mathrm{mA}\\)</p><p>The current flows from left to right, that is, in the opposite direction to the electron flow.</p>",
