    "content": "<p>\\(R=\\rho\\frac{L}{A}\\) ...(12.3)</p><p>Where ρ (Greek LETTER &#x27;Rho&#x27;) is a constant and is known as resistivity or specific resistance of the material.</p><p>The specific resistance of a material is the resistance offered by 1m length of wire of a material having an area of cross-section of 1m². A wire of 1 metre length is shown in figure 12.4. The unit of resistivity is ohm-meter (Ω.m). The resistivity of a substance varies over a wide range. To give an idea to the reader, the following table may be referred.</p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 480 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"FIGURE 12.4: Cross-section area of a material\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:480px;height:auto\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M92 65H385V137H92Z\" fill=\"#dbeafe\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"92\" cy=\"101\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#7dd3fc\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><ellipse cx=\"385\" cy=\"101\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"36\" fill=\"#bfdbfe\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M92 164H385M92 158V171M385 158V171\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><text x=\"238\" y=\"190\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"16\">1 m</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\">1 m²</text><text x=\"391\" y=\"54\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"15\">1 m²</text><text x=\"250\" y=\"30\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"17\">Cross-section area of a material</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"13\">FIGURE 12.4</text></svg>",
    "theory": "\\(R=\\rho\\frac{L}{A}\\) ...(12.3)\nWhere ρ (Greek LETTER 'Rho') is a constant and is known as resistivity or specific resistance of the material.\nThe specific resistance of a material is the resistance offered by 1m length of wire of a material having an area of cross-section of 1m². A wire of 1 metre length is shown in figure 12.4. The unit of resistivity is ohm-meter (Ω.m). The resistivity of a substance varies over a wide range. To give an idea to the reader, the following table may be referred.",
