    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>POSITIVE TEMPERATURE COEFFICIENT (PTC) THERMISTOR:</p><p>PTC thermistor is generally used for fuse purpose. The resistance of PTC thermistor increases with increase in temperature and when temperature decreases, its resistance decreases. One of the properties of PTC thermistors is that when an excessively large current flows, they generate heat by themselves and become highly resistive. With this property, they are used as overcurrent protection devices. They are used as timing devices in televisions. They are also used as heater in automotive industry to provide additional heat inside cabin with diesel engine or to heat diesel in cold climatic conditions before engine injection.</p>",
    "theory": "POSITIVE TEMPERATURE COEFFICIENT (PTC) THERMISTOR:\nPTC thermistor is generally used for fuse purpose. The resistance of PTC thermistor increases with increase in temperature and when temperature decreases, its resistance decreases. One of the properties of PTC thermistors is that when an excessively large current flows, they generate heat by themselves and become highly resistive. With this property, they are used as overcurrent protection devices. They are used as timing devices in televisions. They are also used as heater in automotive industry to provide additional heat inside cabin with diesel engine or to heat diesel in cold climatic conditions before engine injection.",
