    "content": "<p>SOURCES OF e.m.f.</p><p>The work done by emf on charge carriers in its interior must be derived from a source of energy. There are many sources of e.m.f. A few examples are</p><p>1. Batteries or cells convert chemical energy into electrical energy.</p><p>2. Electrical generators convert mechanical energy into electrical energy.</p><p>3. Thermocouples convert heat energy into electrical energy.</p><p>4. Radiant (a solar cell) converts sunlight directly into electrical energy.</p>",
    "theory": "SOURCES OF e.m.f.\nThe work done by emf on charge carriers in its interior must be derived from a source of energy. There are many sources of e.m.f. A few examples are\n1. Batteries or cells convert chemical energy into electrical energy.\n2. Electrical generators convert mechanical energy into electrical energy.\n3. Thermocouples convert heat energy into electrical energy.\n4. Radiant (a solar cell) converts sunlight directly into electrical energy.",
