    "id": "phys12-unit12-example126-energy-cost70",
    "title": "Example 12.6 — monthly electricity cost",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>EXAMPLE 12.6</p><p>The following are the details of load and a circuit connected through a supply meter.</p><p>(i) Six lamps of 40 watts each working for 4 hours per day.</p><p>(ii) Two fluorescent tubes 125 watts each working for 2 hours per day.</p><p>(iii) 1000 watts heater working for 3 hours per day.</p><p>Find the cost of electrical energy consumed in 30 days of a month when the rate of electricity is 7.0 Rs per unit.</p><p>SOLUTION</p><p>Total watts for lamps \\(=40\\times6=240\\) watts</p><p>Total watts for tubes \\(=125\\times2=250\\) watts</p><p>Heater = 1000 watts</p><p>Energy consumed per day</p><p>\\(=(250\\times4)+(250\\times2)+(1000\\times3)\\)</p><p>\\(=4460\\) watt hours</p><p>\\(=4.46\\text{ kWh}\\)</p><p>Total energy consumed in the month of June</p><p>\\(=4.46\\times30=133.8\\text{ kWh}\\)</p><p>Bill for the month of June</p><p>\\(=7\\times133.8=936.6\\text{ Rs}\\)</p>",
    "theory": "EXAMPLE 12.6\nThe following are the details of load and a circuit connected through a supply meter.\n(i) Six lamps of 40 watts each working for 4 hours per day.\n(ii) Two fluorescent tubes 125 watts each working for 2 hours per day.\n(iii) 1000 watts heater working for 3 hours per day.\nFind the cost of electrical energy consumed in 30 days of a month when the rate of electricity is 7.0 Rs per unit.\nSOLUTION\nTotal watts for lamps \\(=40\\times6=240\\) watts\nTotal watts for tubes \\(=125\\times2=250\\) watts\nHeater = 1000 watts\nEnergy consumed per day\n\\(=(250\\times4)+(250\\times2)+(1000\\times3)\\)\n\\(=4460\\) watt hours\n\\(=4.46\\text{ kWh}\\)\nTotal energy consumed in the month of June\n\\(=4.46\\times30=133.8\\text{ kWh}\\)\nBill for the month of June\n\\(=7\\times133.8=936.6\\text{ Rs}\\)",
