    "id": "phys12-unit12-thermoelectric-variation73",
    "title": "12.12 Variation in thermoelectric emf with temperature",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>12.12 VARIATION IN THERMOELECTRIC e.m.f. WITH TEMPERATURE</p><p>Keeping the junction B at 0°C, the temperature of junction A is increased. When both the junctions are at the same temperature, there is no thermo e.m.f. When the temperature at one junction is cold while at the other end is increased the thermo e.m.f. also increases with temperature and reaches a maximum value at a certain temperature, called the neutral temperature Tₙ.</p><p>The value of the neutral temperature is constant for a thermocouple, depends on the nature of materials and is independent of the temperature of the cold junction. As the temperature of the hot junction is increased, the thermo e.m.f. starts decreasing instead of increasing.</p><p>The particular temperature at which the thermo e.m.f. becomes zero is called the inversion temperature Figure 12.12 (b). The graph shows the variation of the thermo e.m.f. with the temperature of hot junction, with the cold junction.</p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 540 245\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"FIGURE 12.12\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:540px;height:auto\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M85 190V42M85 190H470\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M88 187C130 112 175 57 235 57C300 58 350 116 425 187\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M235 58H85M235 58V190\" stroke=\"#94a3b8\" stroke-dasharray=\"5 4\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M80 48l5-10 5 10M464 185l10 5-10 5\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"36\" font-size=\"12\">Thermo emf</text><text x=\"430\" y=\"218\" font-size=\"12\">Temperature T</text><text x=\"240\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"11\">Tₙ</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"229\" font-size=\"11\">Neutral temperature</text><text x=\"170\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"12\">(b) Variation for copper-iron thermocouple</text><text x=\"395\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"13\">FIGURE 12.12</text></svg>",
