    "content": "<p>CONCEPTUAL QUESTIONS</p><p>1. A heavy duty battery of a truck maintains a current of 3 A for 24 hour. How much charge flows from the battery during this time?</p><p>2. While analysing a circuit the internal resistance of e.m.f. sources are ignored why?</p><p>3. If aluminium and copper wires of the same length have the same resistance, which has the larger diameter? Why?</p><p>4. Under what circumstances can the terminal P.D. of a battery exceed its e.m.f.?</p><p>5. What is the difference between an e.m.f. and a P.D.?</p><p>6. How are the loop rule and junction rule based on the conservation of energy principle?</p><p>7. Why is a rise in temperature of a conductor accompanied by a rise in the resistance?</p><p>8. Does the direction of e.m.f. provided by a battery depend on the direction of current flow through the battery?</p><p>9. Voltages are always measured between two points. Why?</p><p>10. Is every e.m.f. a potential difference? Is every potential difference an e.m.f.?</p><p>11. How much charge flows in a pocket calculator each minute when the current is 0.0001 A?</p><p>12. When a Wheatstone bridge is balanced, then no current flows through the galvanometer. Why?</p>",
