    "content": "<p>NUMERICAL PROBLEMS</p><p>1. A battery has an e.m.f. of 12.8 V and supplies a current of 3.2 A. What is the resistance of the circuit? How many coulombs leave the battery in 5 minutes?</p><p>Answer (4 Ω, 1200 C)</p><p>2. Two light bulbs designed for 120-V use are rated at 40 W and 60 W. Which light bulb has the greater filament resistance? Why?</p><p>Answer (240 Ω, 360 Ω)</p><p>3. A carbon electrode has a resistance of 0.125 Ω at 20 °C. The temperature coefficient of carbon is −0.0005 at 20 °C. What will be the resistance of the electrode at 85 °C?</p><p>Answer (0.12 Ω)</p><p>4. Calculate the resistance of wire 10 m long that has a diameter of 2 mm and resistivity of 2.63 × 10⁻⁸ Ω m.</p><p>Answer (0.0838 Ω)</p><p>5. A typical 12 V automobile battery has a resistance of 0.012 Ω. What is the terminal voltage of this battery when the starter draws a current of 100 A? Calculate R, Pε, P_R and P_r.</p><p>Answer (10.8 V, 0.108 Ω, 1200 W, 120 W)</p><p>6. A 10 watt resistor has a value of 120 Ω. What is the rated current through the resistor?</p><p>Answer (0.2886 A)</p><p>7. A resistor of 50 Ω has a P.D. of 100 V, D.C. across 1 hour. Calculate (a) Power and (b) Energy.</p><p>Answer ((a) 200 W, (b) 0.72 MJ)</p><p>8. Calculate the current through a single loop circuit if ε = 120 V, R = 1000 Ω and internal resistance r = 0.01 Ω.</p><p>Answer (120 mA)</p>",
    "theory": "NUMERICAL PROBLEMS\n1. A battery has an e.m.f. of 12.8 V and supplies a current of 3.2 A. What is the resistance of the circuit? How many coulombs leave the battery in 5 minutes?\nAnswer (4 Ω, 1200 C)\n2. Two light bulbs designed for 120-V use are rated at 40 W and 60 W. Which light bulb has the greater filament resistance? Why?\nAnswer (240 Ω, 360 Ω)\n3. A carbon electrode has a resistance of 0.125 Ω at 20 °C. The temperature coefficient of carbon is −0.0005 at 20 °C. What will be the resistance of the electrode at 85 °C?\nAnswer (0.12 Ω)\n4. Calculate the resistance of wire 10 m long that has a diameter of 2 mm and resistivity of 2.63 × 10⁻⁸ Ω m.\nAnswer (0.0838 Ω)\n5. A typical 12 V automobile battery has a resistance of 0.012 Ω. What is the terminal voltage of this battery when the starter draws a current of 100 A? Calculate R, Pε, P_R and P_r.\nAnswer (10.8 V, 0.108 Ω, 1200 W, 120 W)\n6. A 10 watt resistor has a value of 120 Ω. What is the rated current through the resistor?\nAnswer (0.2886 A)\n7. A resistor of 50 Ω has a P.D. of 100 V, D.C. across 1 hour. Calculate (a) Power and (b) Energy.\nAnswer ((a) 200 W, (b) 0.72 MJ)\n8. Calculate the current through a single loop circuit if ε = 120 V, R = 1000 Ω and internal resistance r = 0.01 Ω.\nAnswer (120 mA)",
