      "NUMERICAL PROBLEMS",
      "1. At what distance from a long straight wire carrying a current of 10 A is the magnetic field equal to Earth’s magnetic field of 5 × 10⁻⁵ T? (Answer: 0.04 m)",
      "2. A long solenoid having 1000 turns uniformly distributed over a length of 0.5 m produces a magnetic field of 2.5 × 10⁻³ T at its center. Find the current in the solenoid. (Answer: 1 A)",
      "3. A proton moving at right angles to a magnetic field of 0.1 T experiences a force of 2 × 10⁻¹² N. What is the proton’s speed? (Answer: 1.3 × 10⁸ m/s)",
      "4. An 8 MeV proton enters perpendicularly into a uniform magnetic field of 2.5 T. (a) Find the force on the electron. (b) What is the radius of the path of the proton? (Answer: 1.6 × 10⁻¹¹ N, 0.17 m)",
