    "id": "phys13-right-hand-rule-I91",
    "title": "Right-hand Rule I — magnetic field around a wire",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>RIGHT-HAND RULE I FOR THE MAGNETIC FIELD FROM A CURRENT-CARRYING WIRE</p><p>Put your thumb in the direction of current and curl your fingers around the wire; the curled fingers will show the direction of the magnetic field. This rule is for the direction of conventional current or flow of positive charges. For electronic current flow, the same rule is applied but with the left hand.</p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 560 285\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Figure 13.3: thumb points along current; curled fingers show the magnetic field direction.\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:560px;height:auto\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path d=\"M280 238V66\" stroke=\"#7c2d12\" stroke-width=\"12\"/><path d=\"M280 48l-15 25h30z\" fill=\"#16a34a\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"16\">I — Current</text><ellipse cx=\"280\" cy=\"151\" rx=\"88\" ry=\"44\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M355 124l16 5-14 9\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><path d=\"M205 178l-16-5 14-9\" fill=\"#2563eb\"/><text x=\"383\" y=\"151\" font-size=\"16\">B — Magnetic field</text></svg>",
    "theory": "RIGHT-HAND RULE I FOR THE MAGNETIC FIELD FROM A CURRENT-CARRYING WIRE\nPut your thumb in the direction of current and curl your fingers around the wire; the curled fingers will show the direction of the magnetic field. This rule is for the direction of conventional current or flow of positive charges. For electronic current flow, the same rule is applied but with the left hand.",
