        "text": "Ampere law is the relation between magnetic field and current near a current-carrying conductor. When no current is present in the wire, all compass needles point in the same direction (toward the Earth’s north pole). When the wire carries a strong current, the compass needles deflect in a direction tangent to the circle, which is the direction of the magnetic field created by the current. Now consider a test point P located at distance r from the current-carrying conductor, where we want to find the magnitude of magnetic induction B as shown in Figure 13.10. At point P, magnetic induction is directly proportional to the current I flowing through the conductor and inversely proportional to the distance r from the wire.",
        "english": "Ampere law is the relation between magnetic field and current near a current-carrying conductor. When no current is present in the wire, all compass needles point in the same direction (toward the Earth’s north pole). When the wire carries a strong current, the compass needles deflect in a direction tangent to the circle, which is the direction of the magnetic field created by the current. Now consider a test point P located at distance r from the current-carrying conductor, where we want to find the magnitude of magnetic induction B as shown in Figure 13.10. At point P, magnetic induction is directly proportional to the current I flowing through the conductor and inversely proportional to the distance r from the wire.",
        "urdu": "ایمپیئر کا قانون کرنٹ بردار موصل کے قریب مقناطیسی میدان اور برقی رو کا تعلق ہے۔ تار میں رو نہ ہو تو قطب نما کی تمام سوئیاں ایک ہی سمت (زمین کے شمالی قطب کی طرف) اشارہ کرتی ہیں۔ تار میں تیز رو گزرنے پر سوئیاں دائرے کے مماس سمت میں مڑتی ہیں، جو رو کے پیدا کردہ مقناطیسی میدان کی سمت ہے۔ اب تار سے فاصلے r پر واقع آزمائشی نقطے P پر غور کریں جہاں شکل 13.10 کے مطابق مقناطیسی القا B کی مقدار معلوم کرنی ہے۔ نقطہ P پر B، تار میں بہنے والی رو I کے براہ راست اور تار سے فاصلے r کے الٹ متناسب ہے۔",
