    "id": "phys13-example132-setup97",
    "title": "Example 13.2 — magnetic field midway between two wires",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>EXAMPLE 13.2 — MAGNETIC FIELD BETWEEN CURRENT-CARRYING WIRES</p><p>Two long parallel wires 6 cm apart carry currents of 8 A and 2 A in the same direction. What is the magnitude of the magnetic field midway between them?</p><p>GIVEN</p><p>Current due to wire 1: I₁ = 8 A; current due to wire 2: I₂ = 2 A.</p><p>At midway between wires, r₁ = r₂ = 6 cm/2 = 0.03 m.</p><p>REQUIRED</p><p>Net magnetic field B_net = ?</p>",
    "theory": "EXAMPLE 13.2 — MAGNETIC FIELD BETWEEN CURRENT-CARRYING WIRES\nTwo long parallel wires 6 cm apart carry currents of 8 A and 2 A in the same direction. What is the magnitude of the magnetic field midway between them?\nGIVEN\nCurrent due to wire 1: I₁ = 8 A; current due to wire 2: I₂ = 2 A.\nAt midway between wires, r₁ = r₂ = 6 cm/2 = 0.03 m.\nREQUIRED\nNet magnetic field B_net = ?",
