    "content": "<p>If the electric and magnetic fields are applied perpendicular to each other and adjusted such that the magnitude of electric force is equal but direction is opposite to the magnetic force as shown in Figure 13.21, then</p><p>Since F_electric = qE and F_magnetic = qvB,</p><p>Therefore qE = qvB</p><p>v = E/B ...(13.10)</p><p>If the beam of charged particles moving with different velocities passes through a velocity selector, only those particles will pass straight through the device which have velocities equal to the ratio of electric to the magnetic field. Particles moving slower than this speed will be deflected in the direction of electric force, and those having greater speeds will be deflected in the direction of magnetic force.</p>",
