    "title": "Converting a galvanometer into a voltmeter — introduction",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>B. CONVERSION OF GALVANOMETER INTO VOLTMETER</p><p>A voltmeter is a measuring instrument used to measure potential difference in a circuit.</p><p>A voltmeter is a modified form of galvanometer used to measure electric potential. A galvanometer is converted into a voltmeter by connecting a high resistance in series with it.</p><p>FIGURE 13.27 — (a) Voltmeter. (b) Internal circuit with high resistance R_h.</p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 700 340\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Figure 13.26/13.27: translated ammeter or voltmeter internal circuit diagram.\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:700px;height:auto\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#fff\"/><circle cx=\"350\" cy=\"165\" r=\"112\" fill=\"#fef08a\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"5\" stroke-dasharray=\"8 5\"/><circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"165\" r=\"28\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"268\" y=\"172\" font-size=\"18\">G</text><path d=\"M308 165H354l10-16 18 32 18-32 18 32 18-16H480\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"115\">R_g</text><text x=\"382\" y=\"115\">R_h</text><text x=\"300\" y=\"40\">Voltmeter</text><path d=\"M180 165H250M480 165H540M180 165V260H540V165\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"4\"/></svg>",
