    "theory": "C. RESISTANCE MEASUREMENT\nTo measure voltage, the selector switch is turned to measure ohms. The leads are connected across the resistance to be measured as shown in Figure 13.31. The battery supplies current to the galvanometer for deflection. Since the amount of current through the galvanometer depends upon the external resistance, the scale can be calibrated in ohms.\nFIGURE 13.31 — AVO meter switch turned to resistance measurement.",
