    "id": "phys13-digital-multimeter-and-figure1332-120",
    "title": "Digital multimeters and Figure 13.32",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>The amount of deflection in the galvanometer now shows the resistance directly. The ohm-meter reading does not depend on the polarity of the terminal leads, because the direction of current through the galvanometer is determined by the polarity of the battery.</p><p>I. DIGITAL MULTI-METERS</p><p>Modern multimeters have a digital display, are accurate, reliable and durable, and have added extra features. They are easy to use because values are displayed automatically in decimal form with proper units. Thus human errors (such as parallax) in reading an ordinary AVO meter are eliminated.</p><p>In these devices, an integrated circuit electronically controls all functions instead of an ordinary galvanometer. Modern digital multimeters use computer software, which provides other functions as well and increases the scope of multimeter use.</p><p>FIGURE 13.32 — Digital multimeter.</p><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 520 420\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Coded vector digital multimeter with display, selector and leads.\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:520px;height:auto\"><rect width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" fill=\"#fff\"/><rect x=\"115\" y=\"25\" width=\"300\" height=\"350\" rx=\"28\" fill=\"#dc2626\" stroke=\"#7f1d1d\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><rect x=\"155\" y=\"55\" width=\"220\" height=\"82\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#d1fae5\" stroke=\"#166534\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><text x=\"175\" y=\"110\" font-size=\"40\" fill=\"#111827\">018.8</text><circle cx=\"265\" cy=\"235\" r=\"80\" fill=\"#111827\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"8\"/><circle cx=\"265\" cy=\"235\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#dc2626\"/><path d=\"M265 235L316 190\" stroke=\"#f8fafc\" stroke-width=\"7\"/><circle cx=\"200\" cy=\"335\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#111827\"/><circle cx=\"330\" cy=\"335\" r=\"12\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M200 335C150 385 420 390 385 320M330 335C400 395 430 370 450 320\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><text x=\"23\" y=\"75\">Display</text><text x=\"365\" y=\"250\">Range selector</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"355\">Leads</text></svg>",
    "theory": "The amount of deflection in the galvanometer now shows the resistance directly. The ohm-meter reading does not depend on the polarity of the terminal leads, because the direction of current through the galvanometer is determined by the polarity of the battery.\nI. DIGITAL MULTI-METERS\nModern multimeters have a digital display, are accurate, reliable and durable, and have added extra features. They are easy to use because values are displayed automatically in decimal form with proper units. Thus human errors (such as parallax) in reading an ordinary AVO meter are eliminated.\nIn these devices, an integrated circuit electronically controls all functions instead of an ordinary galvanometer. Modern digital multimeters use computer software, which provides other functions as well and increases the scope of multimeter use.\nFIGURE 13.32 — Digital multimeter.",
