    "id": "phys13-exercise-multiple-choice-questions1-14-122-123",
    "title": "Unit 13 exercise — multiple-choice questions 1–14",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>CHOOSE THE BEST POSSIBLE ANSWER</p><p>1. A current flows north in a magnetic field that points west. It experiences: A. a force down; B. a force up; C. a force west; D. no force.</p><p>2. Two long, straight wires carry currents in the same direction. The force between the wires is: A. attractive; B. repulsive; C. zero; D. infinite.</p><p>3. One weber is equal to: A. N A²/m; B. N m²/A; C. N A/m; D. N m/A.</p><p>4. Magnetic flux is maximum if the angle between magnetic-field strength and the area vector is: A. 0°; B. 45°; C. 60°; D. 90°.</p><p>5. Ampere’s law is applied over any: A. surface; B. closed surface; C. path; D. closed path.</p><p>6. If the number of turns in a solenoid is doubled without changing its length, its self-induction will be: A. four times; B. doubled; C. halved; D. one fourth.</p><p>7. If a charge is at rest in a magnetic field, the force on it is: A. qvB; B. qvB cos θ; C. qvB sin θ; D. zero.</p><p>8. Work done on a charged particle moving in a uniform magnetic field is: A. maximum; B. minimum; C. zero; D. infinite.</p><p>9. The Earth’s northern magnetic pole acts like: A. the north pole of a magnet; B. the south pole of a magnet; C. a positive charge; D. a negative charge.</p><p>10. The pole pieces of a galvanometer magnet are made concave to make the field: A. radial; B. stronger; C. weaker; D. both A and B.</p><p>11. When a small resistance is connected in parallel to a galvanometer, the resulting circuit behaves as a: A. voltmeter; B. ammeter; C. velocity selector; D. AVO meter.</p><p>12. To measure voltage, a voltmeter is connected with the circuit in: A. series; B. parallel; C. perpendicular; D. a straight line.</p><p>13. The resistance of an ideal voltmeter is: A. small; B. large; C. zero; D. infinite.</p><p>14. The torque in a coil can be increased by increasing: A. number of turns; B. current and magnetic field; C. area of coil; D. all of these.</p>",
    "theory": "CHOOSE THE BEST POSSIBLE ANSWER\n1. A current flows north in a magnetic field that points west. It experiences: A. a force down; B. a force up; C. a force west; D. no force.\n2. Two long, straight wires carry currents in the same direction. The force between the wires is: A. attractive; B. repulsive; C. zero; D. infinite.\n3. One weber is equal to: A. N A²/m; B. N m²/A; C. N A/m; D. N m/A.\n4. Magnetic flux is maximum if the angle between magnetic-field strength and the area vector is: A. 0°; B. 45°; C. 60°; D. 90°.\n5. Ampere’s law is applied over any: A. surface; B. closed surface; C. path; D. closed path.\n6. If the number of turns in a solenoid is doubled without changing its length, its self-induction will be: A. four times; B. doubled; C. halved; D. one fourth.\n7. If a charge is at rest in a magnetic field, the force on it is: A. qvB; B. qvB cos θ; C. qvB sin θ; D. zero.\n8. Work done on a charged particle moving in a uniform magnetic field is: A. maximum; B. minimum; C. zero; D. infinite.\n9. The Earth’s northern magnetic pole acts like: A. the north pole of a magnet; B. the south pole of a magnet; C. a positive charge; D. a negative charge.\n10. The pole pieces of a galvanometer magnet are made concave to make the field: A. radial; B. stronger; C. weaker; D. both A and B.\n11. When a small resistance is connected in parallel to a galvanometer, the resulting circuit behaves as a: A. voltmeter; B. ammeter; C. velocity selector; D. AVO meter.\n12. To measure voltage, a voltmeter is connected with the circuit in: A. series; B. parallel; C. perpendicular; D. a straight line.\n13. The resistance of an ideal voltmeter is: A. small; B. large; C. zero; D. infinite.\n14. The torque in a coil can be increased by increasing: A. number of turns; B. current and magnetic field; C. area of coil; D. all of these.",
