        "originalText": "Here N = 1 and flux Φ = BA cos θ. We have θ = 0° and cos θ = 1 because B is perpendicular to A. Since B is uniform, the change in flux is ΔΦ = Δ(BA) = BΔA. The area enclosed by circuit MNRS changes by ΔA = ℓΔx.",
