        "text": "MAX PLANCK (1858–1947) — Planck was German. His work on the spectral distribution of radiation led to quantum theory and was honored with the 1918 Nobel Prize. Figure 18.7 compares experimental black-body data with Planck’s theory and the classical Rayleigh–Jeans curve.",
        "english": "MAX PLANCK (1858–1947) — Planck was German. His work on the spectral distribution of radiation led to quantum theory and was honored with the 1918 Nobel Prize. Figure 18.7 compares experimental black-body data with Planck’s theory and the classical Rayleigh–Jeans curve.",
