        "english": "EXAMPLE 18.2 — Human skin is approximately 35°C. Find the wavelength of the peak in radiation emitted by the skin. Given Wien’s constant 0.2898×10⁻² m·K and T=35+273=308 K. Using λ_maxT=constant, λ_max=(0.2898×10⁻² m·K)/308 K=9.409×10⁻⁶ m=9.4 μm.",
