        "english": "FIRST PHOTOELECTRIC EXPERIMENT — Adjust the potential difference V so the collector is slightly negative relative to the emitter; this slows the ejected electrons. V is varied until a value called the stopping potential V₀ makes the sensitive ammeter reading just zero. At V=V₀, the most energetic electrons are turned back before reaching the collector. Their maximum kinetic energy is KE_max=eV₀ (Equation 18.9), where e is elementary charge. For a given light frequency, KE_max does not depend on light intensity.",
