    "content": "<p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 4 — What is the photoelectric effect? Discuss the failure of classical physics and the success of the photon concept in explaining it.</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 5 — What is the Compton effect? Develop a mathematical relation for the Compton wave shift.</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 6 — Write a note on pair production and annihilation of matter.</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 7 — What is the de Broglie hypothesis? Describe an experiment showing that particles have wave characteristics.</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 8 — What is meant by wave-particle duality? Explain.</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 9 — State and explain Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle. Justify its validity by a thought experiment.</p><p>NUMERICAL PROBLEM 1 — A spaceship’s length is measured as exactly one-third of its proper length. Find its speed relative to the observer. Printed answer: 0.9428c.</p><p>NUMERICAL PROBLEM 2 — A pendulum’s period is 3 s in its inertial rest frame. What period is measured by an observer moving at 0.95c relative to it? Printed answer: 9.6 s.</p><p>NUMERICAL PROBLEM 3 — A metal with work function 3.0 eV is illuminated by wavelength 3×10⁻⁷ m. Find (a) threshold frequency, (b) maximum photoelectron energy and (c) stopping potential. Printed answers: (a) 0.72×10¹⁵ Hz, (b) 1.16 eV, (c) 1.16 V.</p><p>NUMERICAL PROBLEM 4 — A 50 keV X-ray is scattered through 90°. Find its energy after Compton scattering. Printed answer: 45.5 keV.</p><p>NUMERICAL PROBLEM 5 — An electron speed is 5×10³ m·s⁻¹ with accuracy 0.003%. Find the uncertainty in its position. Printed answer: 4.84×10⁻³ m.</p>",
    "theory": "COMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 4 — What is the photoelectric effect? Discuss the failure of classical physics and the success of the photon concept in explaining it.\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 5 — What is the Compton effect? Develop a mathematical relation for the Compton wave shift.\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 6 — Write a note on pair production and annihilation of matter.\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 7 — What is the de Broglie hypothesis? Describe an experiment showing that particles have wave characteristics.\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 8 — What is meant by wave-particle duality? Explain.\nCOMPREHENSIVE QUESTION 9 — State and explain Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle. Justify its validity by a thought experiment.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEM 1 — A spaceship’s length is measured as exactly one-third of its proper length. Find its speed relative to the observer. Printed answer: 0.9428c.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEM 2 — A pendulum’s period is 3 s in its inertial rest frame. What period is measured by an observer moving at 0.95c relative to it? Printed answer: 9.6 s.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEM 3 — A metal with work function 3.0 eV is illuminated by wavelength 3×10⁻⁷ m. Find (a) threshold frequency, (b) maximum photoelectron energy and (c) stopping potential. Printed answers: (a) 0.72×10¹⁵ Hz, (b) 1.16 eV, (c) 1.16 V.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEM 4 — A 50 keV X-ray is scattered through 90°. Find its energy after Compton scattering. Printed answer: 45.5 keV.\nNUMERICAL PROBLEM 5 — An electron speed is 5×10³ m·s⁻¹ with accuracy 0.003%. Find the uncertainty in its position. Printed answer: 4.84×10⁻³ m.",
