    "paragraphs": [
      "UNIT 15 KEY POINTS — Alternating voltage: voltage whose polarity changes at regular intervals. Sinusoidal voltage: V=V_m sinωt. Waveform: graph of instantaneous voltage/current versus time. Cycle: one complete positive and negative set. Time period: time for one cycle. Frequency f: cycles per second. Average value: average over a period. Phase difference: phase offset between same-frequency alternating quantities. Phasor: rotating line representing a sinusoidal quantity. Inductive reactance X_L: opposition by an inductor to charge flow. Peak value: maximum waveform value. Resonance: an A.C. circuit with reactive L and C elements whose power factor is unity.",
      "EXERCISE — CHOOSE THE BEST POSSIBLE ANSWER (questions 1–8). 1. A sine wave has r.m.s. value 100 A; its peak value is (A)70.7 A (B)141.4 A (C)150 A (D)282.8 A. 2. A 50 Hz sine wave has angular frequency (A)100π (B)50π (C)25π (D)5π rad/s. 3. Power factor of a purely resistive circuit: (A)zero (B)unity (C)lagging (D)leading. 4. A capacitor is a perfect insulator for (A)D.C. (B)A.C. (C)both D.C. and A.C. (D)induced e.m.f. 5. Peak current 5√2 A; mean-square current is (A)5 A (B)2.5 A (C)5√2 A (D)5². 6. In a choke coil, X_L and R are related as (A)X_L=R (B)X_L≪R (C)X_L≫R (D)X_L=∞. 7. At resonance, current-voltage phase difference is (A)0 (B)π (C)−π (D)π/2. 8. An A.C. system generates a sine waveform because (A)it is easy to draw (B)it causes least circuit disturbance (C)it is nature’s standard (D)other waves cannot be produced easily."
    ]
