        "english": "EXAMPLE 15.3 GIVEN — Inductance L = 60 mH; current I = 0.2 sin(377t − 25°) A. REQUIRED — Write the mathematical expression for voltage V across the inductor. SOLUTION — Xₗ = 2πfL = 377 × 60 × 10⁻³ = 22.62 Ω. Vₘ = IₘXₗ = 0.2 × 22.62 = 4.5 V. Voltage leads current by 90°, so add 90° to its phase: V = Vₘ sin(377t − 25° + 90°) = 4.5 sin(377t + 65°) V.",
