        "english": "EXAMPLE 15.5 — A coil with resistance 7 Ω and inductance 31.8 mH is connected to a 220 V, 50 Hz supply. Find circuit current, phase angle, power factor and power consumed. GIVEN: L = 31.8 mH; V = 220 V; R = 7 Ω; f = 50 Hz. SOLUTION: X_L = 2πfL = 2π×50×31.8×10⁻³ = 10 Ω. Z = √(R²+X_L²) = √(7²+10²) = 12.2 Ω. I = V/Z = 220/12.2 = 18.03 A. tanφ = X_L/R = 10/7; φ = tan⁻¹(10/7) = 55° lag. Power factor cos55° = 0.573 lag. P = VI cosφ = 220×18.03×0.573 = 2272.8 W.",
