        "originalText": "INFRARED — Infrared wavelengths are longer than visible light, from about 0.7 μm to 1 mm. Atoms or molecules emit it during rotational or vibrational changes. It transfers heat and is also called thermal radiation; objects at about 3–3000 K emit their strongest thermal radiation in the infrared. Home remote controls use invisible infrared pulses; Figure 15.26 shows an infrared image of the Milky Way.",
