        "text": "X-RAYS — Typical wavelengths are about 0.01–10 nm. They can arise from inner-electron transitions or from deceleration of charged particles such as electrons. X-rays pass through soft tissue but are stopped by bone and other solid matter, making them useful in medical diagnosis.",
        "english": "X-RAYS — Typical wavelengths are about 0.01–10 nm. They can arise from inner-electron transitions or from deceleration of charged particles such as electrons. X-rays pass through soft tissue but are stopped by bone and other solid matter, making them useful in medical diagnosis.",
