    "content": "<p>EXERCISE — CHOOSE THE BEST POSSIBLE ANSWER (questions 9–15). 9. An alternating voltage is 20 sin157t. Its frequency is (A)50 Hz (B)25 Hz (C)100 Hz (D)75 Hz. 10. In an LR circuit, which statement is correct? (A)L and R oppose each other (B)R increases with frequency (C)inductive reactance increases with frequency (D)inductive reactance decreases with frequency. 11. An alternating quantity is completely known if we know its (A)maximum value (B)frequency and phase (C)effective value (D)both maximum value and frequency/phase. 12. For electromagnetic waves, Maxwell generalized (A)Gauss’s law for magnetism (B)Gauss’s law for electricity (C)Faraday’s law (D)Ampere’s law. 13. An electromagnetic wave goes from air to glass; which does not change? (A)radio waves (B)X-rays (C)ultraviolet radiation (D)ultrasound waves. 14. If current and voltage are in phase, power factor is (A)0 (B)1 (C)−1 (D)2. 15. With increased A.C. supply frequency, the impedance of an RLC series circuit (A)remains constant (B)increases (C)decreases (D)only capacitive reactance X_C decreases.</p><p>CONCEPTUAL QUESTIONS (1–7). 1. Sketch induced e.m.f. in an inductive coil against rate of change of current; what does the gradient signify? 2. A.C. generator current and voltage can be positive or negative; why can power never be negative when connected to a resistor? 3. What determines the gradient of inductive reactance versus frequency? 4. How does doubling frequency affect (a) inductor reactance and (b) capacitor reactance? 5. If a sine wave peak is 1,000 V, what is its effective value? 6. Show that reactance is measured in ohms for inductors and capacitors. 7. What is the principle of ECG?</p><p>COMPREHENSIVE QUESTIONS (1–3). 1. Define mean, peak and r.m.s. values of sinusoidal current and voltage; derive the mathematical expression for r.m.s. current. 2. A sinusoidal A.C. voltage of angular frequency ω is connected across resistor R. Find expressions for instantaneous voltage, instantaneous current and average power dissipated per cycle. 3. A sinusoidal A.C. voltage of angular frequency ω is connected across capacitor C. Find expressions for instantaneous voltage, instantaneous current and average power dissipated per cycle.</p>",
