        "originalText": "16.2 ELASTIC MODULI — An external force changes an object’s shape or size. Small, temporary deformation that disappears when the force is removed is elastic; if deformation remains, it is plastic. Deformation is described by stress and strain. Within the elastic range, stress/strain is constant and is the elastic modulus (Hooke’s law). The three moduli are Young’s modulus Y, shear/rigidity modulus S and bulk modulus B. The table lists values in Pa, in order Y, B, S: aluminium 7×10¹⁰, 7.5×10¹⁰, 2.5×10¹⁰; brass 9×10¹⁰, 6×10¹⁰, 3.5×10¹⁰; copper 11×10¹⁰, 14×10¹⁰, 4.4×10¹⁰; crown glass 6×10¹⁰, 5×10¹⁰, 2.5×10¹⁰; iron 21×10¹⁰, 16×10¹⁰, 7.7×10¹⁰; lead 1.6×10¹⁰, 4.1×10¹⁰, 0.6×10¹⁰; nickel 21×10¹⁰, 17×10¹⁰, 7.8×10¹⁰; steel 20×10¹⁰, 16×10¹⁰, 7.5×10¹⁰.",
