        "english": "16.2.1 YOUNG’S MODULUS — Young’s modulus describes change in length under deforming force. Consider a rod of length L and cross-sectional area A, clamped at one end and pulled perpendicular to its cross-section; its length increases. Internal forces resist the change and, as the source sentence continues on PDF page 110, “but attain an equilibrium in which the length is (L+ΔL) where ΔL is the change in length.”",
