        "english": "EXAMPLE 16.1 — A 500 N force is applied to one end of a cylindrical steel rod of diameter 50 cm. Find tensile stress. GIVEN: F=500 N; r=D/2=25 cm. SOLUTION: stress=force/area=F/(πr²)=500/[π(25×10⁻²)²]=2.5×10⁵ N m⁻².",
