      "Figure 19.6 contrasts (a) Coulomb force supplying centripetal force and (b) radiation emitted only when an electron jumps from a higher to a lower energy level. POSTULATE 3 — An electron in a stable orbit does not radiate energy. The atom radiates only when the electron jumps from an allowed orbit of higher energy Eₙ to one of lower energy Eₚ. Their energy difference appears as a photon with E=hf: hf=Eₙ−Eₚ (Equation 3).",
      "A. RADII OF QUANTIZED ORBITS — In Bohr’s model electrons may orbit only at certain specific distances from the nucleus. These radii are integral multiples of the smallest permitted orbit radius, so the orbits are quantized. From Postulate 1, mv²/rₙ=ke²/rₙ², or mv²=ke²/rₙ (Equation 4). From Postulate 2, mvrₙ=n h/(2π), or v=n h/(2π m rₙ) (Equation 5). Substitution begins at the bottom of page 304 and continues on PDF page 159."
