      "11. In neon, the 20.66-eV level can undergo lasing action to the 18.70-eV level. What is the energy of the resulting photons?\nA. 20.66 eV\nB. 18.70 eV\nC. 39.36 eV\nD. 1.96 eV",
      "12. In connection with inner shell transition the symbol Lβ refers to X-ray emission associated with an electron going from\nA. n=3 to n=1\nB. n=4 to n=1\nC. n=4 to n=2\nD. n=5 to n=3",
