        "text": "The reactor is subcritical when, on average, the neutrons from each fission trigger less than one subsequent fission. In a subcritical reactor, the chain reaction is not self-sustaining and eventually stops. When the neutrons from each fission trigger more than one additional fission, the reactor is supercritical. During a supercritical condition, the energy released by a reactor increases. If left unchecked, the increasing energy can lead to a partial or total meltdown of the reactor core.",
