    "id": "phys20-glossary-tail-and-author-profiles-384",
    "title": "Final glossary entries and authors’ profiles",
    "kind": "book_back_matter",
    "content": "<p>Myelin: a white tissue forming an insulating sheath (myelin sheath) around certain nerve fibres. Damage to the myelin sheath causes neurological disease, as in multiple sclerosis.</p><p>Motor: a device that changes electrical energy into mechanical energy.</p><p>Muon: a negatively charged subatomic particle, with the same charge as an electron.</p><p>Ohm: unit of resistance.</p><p>Ohm’s Law: current is directly proportional to voltage and inversely proportional to resistance.</p><p>Permanent Magnets: it retain their magnetism after a magnetizing force is removed.</p><p>Resistance : the restriction to the flow of electrons.</p><p>RMS Value: Root Mean Square Current is also referred to as effective current and is the square root of the average of all the instantaneous currents.</p><p>Single-Phase: a continuous single alternating current cycle.</p><p>Spectrum: spectrum means set of frequencies absorbed or emitted by a substance.</p><p>Terrestrial sources: sources that are existing or originating inside the limits of the earth.</p><p>Three-Phase: a continuous series of three overlapping AC cycles offset by 120 degrees.</p><p>Transformer: a device used to raise (step up) or lower (step down) a voltage level.</p><p>Ventricle: a chamber of the heart that receives blood from an atrium and pumps it to the arteries.</p><p>Voltage Drop: voltage value as measured across each resistor or load.</p><p>Voltmeter: a device to measure voltage.</p><p>Waveform: the shape of the curve obtained by plotting the instantaneous values of voltage or current as ordinate against time as abscissa is called its waveform or wave shape.</p><p>Watt: the basic unit of power, indicating the amount of work accomplished when one volt causes one ampere to pass through a circuit.</p><p>Authors Profile</p><p>Shaukat Ali Taran did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1988. He also did Master in Education. He is the author and editor of many books of physics. He has 25 years teaching experience in different colleges, including Cadet College, Kohat. Currently, he is working as a Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Timergara (Dir Lower).</p><p>Shadab Gul did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1996. He taught various classes for more than 20 years at school as well as college level. Currently he is working as Assistant Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Lakki Marwat.</p><p>Abdul Baseer did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1990. Currently he is working as a professor in Edwardes College, Peshawer.</p><p>Abdur-Rehman did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 2008. He taught Physics in various private and govt institutions. Currently he is working as a Lecturer in Durrani School and College, Peshawer.</p><p>Dr. Muhammad Naeem Khalid remained Chairman of Physics Department, Islamia College, Peshawer.</p><p>Aamir Ullah Khan has obtained MS - Physics and is currently working as ‘Director’ at Pakistan Virtual College, Hayatabad Peshawar.</p><p>He is the co-author of general science textbooks for grade 6, grade 7 and grade 8 under the National Book Foundation. He is also the co-author of physics textbooks for grade 9, grade 10 and grade 11 of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board, Peshawar.</p><p>Hafiz Mehar Elahi did MS/M.Phil Physics from Qurtuba University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar. Recently honoured with Best Chaperone Awar[clipped at source edge] by GIK Institute of Sciences and Information Technology. He got First position i[clipped at source edge] BS-Physics from Govt College Peshawar in 2014 affiliated with UOP.Currently he i[clipped at source edge] working as Lecturer in Physics at Peshawar Model Degree, College.</p>",
    "theory": "Myelin: a white tissue forming an insulating sheath (myelin sheath) around certain nerve fibres. Damage to the myelin sheath causes neurological disease, as in multiple sclerosis.\nMotor: a device that changes electrical energy into mechanical energy.\nMuon: a negatively charged subatomic particle, with the same charge as an electron.\nOhm: unit of resistance.\nOhm’s Law: current is directly proportional to voltage and inversely proportional to resistance.\nPermanent Magnets: it retain their magnetism after a magnetizing force is removed.\nResistance : the restriction to the flow of electrons.\nRMS Value: Root Mean Square Current is also referred to as effective current and is the square root of the average of all the instantaneous currents.\nSingle-Phase: a continuous single alternating current cycle.\nSpectrum: spectrum means set of frequencies absorbed or emitted by a substance.\nTerrestrial sources: sources that are existing or originating inside the limits of the earth.\nThree-Phase: a continuous series of three overlapping AC cycles offset by 120 degrees.\nTransformer: a device used to raise (step up) or lower (step down) a voltage level.\nVentricle: a chamber of the heart that receives blood from an atrium and pumps it to the arteries.\nVoltage Drop: voltage value as measured across each resistor or load.\nVoltmeter: a device to measure voltage.\nWaveform: the shape of the curve obtained by plotting the instantaneous values of voltage or current as ordinate against time as abscissa is called its waveform or wave shape.\nWatt: the basic unit of power, indicating the amount of work accomplished when one volt causes one ampere to pass through a circuit.\nAuthors Profile\nShaukat Ali Taran did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1988. He also did Master in Education. He is the author and editor of many books of physics. He has 25 years teaching experience in different colleges, including Cadet College, Kohat. Currently, he is working as a Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Timergara (Dir Lower).\nShadab Gul did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1996. He taught various classes for more than 20 years at school as well as college level. Currently he is working as Assistant Professor in Government Post Graduate College, Lakki Marwat.\nAbdul Baseer did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 1990. Currently he is working as a professor in Edwardes College, Peshawer.\nAbdur-Rehman did his M.Sc in Physics from University of Peshawer in 2008. He taught Physics in various private and govt institutions. Currently he is working as a Lecturer in Durrani School and College, Peshawer.\nDr. Muhammad Naeem Khalid remained Chairman of Physics Department, Islamia College, Peshawer.\nAamir Ullah Khan has obtained MS - Physics and is currently working as ‘Director’ at Pakistan Virtual College, Hayatabad Peshawar.\nHe is the co-author of general science textbooks for grade 6, grade 7 and grade 8 under the National Book Foundation. He is also the co-author of physics textbooks for grade 9, grade 10 and grade 11 of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Textbook Board, Peshawar.\nHafiz Mehar Elahi did MS/M.Phil Physics from Qurtuba University of Science and Information Technology, Peshawar. Recently honoured with Best Chaperone Awar[clipped at source edge] by GIK Institute of Sciences and Information Technology. He got First position i[clipped at source edge] BS-Physics from Govt College Peshawar in 2014 affiliated with UOP.Currently he i[clipped at source edge] working as Lecturer in Physics at Peshawar Model Degree, College.",
