      "REQUIRED",
      "P.D. across the parallel plate capacitors \\(V=?\\)",
      "SOLUTION",
      "Charge on capacitor \\(C_1\\) is: \\(Q=C_1V=(6\\times10^{-6})\\times200=0.0012\\mathrm C\\)",
      "The equivalent capacitance of parallel combination of capacitors is",
      "\\(C_{eq}=C_1+C_2=6+3=9\\mu\\mathrm F\\)",
      "The charge 0.0012 C is distributed between the two capacitors to have a common P.D.",
      "P.D. across parallel plate capacitors: \\(V=\\frac Q{C_T}=\\frac{0.0012}{9\\times10^{-6}}=133.3\\mathrm V\\)",
      "[Editorial clarification: the source example statement and GIVEN box specify 3μF, but the GIVEN box later prints 3pF. The solution uses 3μF to obtain 9μF and 133.3V; both printed units are retained.]"
