    "content": "<p>Electrostatic force on charge \\(q_2\\) due to charge \\(q_1\\)= \\(F_{21}=k\\frac{q_1q_2}{r_{12}^2}\\)</p><p>\\(=9.0\\times10^9\\;\\mathrm{N\\,m^2\\,C^{-2}}\\frac{(5\\times10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm C)(10\\times10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm C)}{(6\\times10^{-2}\\,\\mathrm m)^2}\\)</p><p>\\(=9.0\\times10^9\\;\\mathrm{N\\,m^2\\,C^{-2}}\\frac{50\\times10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{C^2}}{36\\times10^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{m^2}}\\)</p><p>Electrostatic force on charge \\(q_2\\) due to \\(q_3\\)=</p><p>\\(F_{23}=9.0\\times10^9\\;\\mathrm{N\\,m^2\\,C^{-2}}\\frac{(10\\times10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm C)(12\\times10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm C)}{4\\times10^{-2}\\,\\mathrm m}\\)</p><p>\\(=9.0\\times10^9\\;\\mathrm{N\\,m^2\\,C^{-2}}\\frac{120\\times10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{C^2}}{16\\times10^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{m^2}}\\)</p><p>\\(=\\frac{1080\\times10^{-3}}{16\\times10^{-4}}\\,\\mathrm N=675\\,\\mathrm N\\)</p><p>The net electrostatic force on charge \\(q_2=F_2=F_{21}-F_{23}\\)</p><p>\\(=675\\,\\mathrm N-125\\,\\mathrm N=550\\,\\mathrm N\\).</p><p>The direction of the net electrostatic force on charge \\(q_2\\) points towards charge \\(q_3\\) (points to the right).</p><p>Source clarification: the first printed substitution for \\(F_{23}\\) omits the square on the distance; the next line correctly uses \\(16\\times10^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{m^2}\\). The printed net-force labels are reversed relative to the subtraction \\(675-125\\). Taking right as positive gives \\(F_2=F_{23}-F_{21}=+550\\,\\mathrm N\\). The original printed statements are retained above; these are textbook typographical inconsistencies.</p><p>\\(=125\\,\\mathrm N\\)</p>",
