    "id": "phys12-front-gauss19",
    "title": "Gauss’s law — flux derivation",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>The electric flux through the small elements \\(\\Delta A_1\\) is</p><p>\\(\\Phi_1=\\vec E_1\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_1=E_1\\Delta A_1\\cos0=E_1\\Delta A_1\\)</p><p>The electric flux through the other small element \\(\\Delta A_2\\) is</p><p>\\(\\Phi_2=\\vec E_2\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_2=E_2\\Delta A_2\\cos0=E_2\\Delta A_2\\)</p><p>Similarly the electric flux through \\(\\Delta A_n\\) is</p><p>\\(\\Phi_n=\\vec E_n\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_n=E_n\\Delta A_n\\cos0=E_n\\Delta A_n\\)</p><p>The total flux through the entire surface is</p><p>\\(\\Phi_E=\\Phi_1+\\Phi_2+\\Phi_3+\\Phi_4+\\ldots+\\Phi_n\\)</p><p>\\(\\Phi_E=\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}E\\Delta A\\) ...(11.12)</p><p>But as electric field intensity E is constant over the surface of sphere</p><p>Therefore,</p><p>\\(\\Phi_E=E\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A\\)</p><p>Since,</p><p>\\(E=\\frac{q}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{1}{r^2}\\)</p><p>Thus the above equation can be written as</p><p>\\(\\Phi_E=\\frac{q}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{1}{r^2}\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A\\)</p><p>\\(\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A=\\) total area enclosed by spherical surface \\(=4\\pi r^2\\)</p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 320 270\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Radial field from positive charge crossing an irregular closed surface\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:320px\"><path d=\"M90 35C140 20 240 45 247 120S203 230 143 220 63 152 71 92 60 43 90 35Z\" fill=\"#a3d977\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M156 130L281.0 130.0\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M281.0 130.0L274.0 133.0L274.0 127.0Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L264.25317547305485 192.5\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M264.25317547305485 192.5L256.6909976465638 191.59807621135332L259.6909976465638 186.40192378864668Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L218.5 238.25317547305482\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M218.5 238.25317547305482L212.40192378864668 233.69099764656374L217.59807621135332 230.69099764656374Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L156.0 255.0\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M156.0 255.0L153.0 248.0L159.0 248.0Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L93.50000000000003 238.25317547305485\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M93.50000000000003 238.25317547305485L94.40192378864671 230.69099764656377L99.59807621135334 233.69099764656377Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L47.74682452694516 192.5\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M47.74682452694516 192.5L52.309002353436235 186.40192378864668L55.309002353436235 191.59807621135332Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L31.0 130.00000000000003\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M31.0 130.00000000000003L38.0 127.00000000000003L38.0 133.00000000000003Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L47.74682452694515 67.50000000000003\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M47.74682452694515 67.50000000000003L55.30900235343622 68.40192378864671L52.30900235343622 73.59807621135334Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L93.49999999999994 21.74682452694519\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M93.49999999999994 21.74682452694519L99.59807621135326 26.30900235343626L94.40192378864663 29.30900235343626Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L155.99999999999997 5.0\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M155.99999999999997 5.0L158.99999999999997 12.0L152.99999999999997 12.0Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L218.5 21.746824526945176\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M218.5 21.746824526945176L217.59807621135332 29.309002353436245L212.40192378864668 26.309002353436245Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><path d=\"M156 130L264.2531754730548 67.49999999999994\" stroke=\"#111827\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M264.2531754730548 67.49999999999994L259.69099764656374 73.59807621135326L256.69099764656374 68.40192378864663Z\" fill=\"#111827\"/><circle cx=\"156\" cy=\"130\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#111827\"/><text x=\"150\" y=\"135\" fill=\"#fff\">+</text></svg><figcaption>FIGURE 11.14: Flux through an irregular close surface</figcaption></figure>",
    "theory": "The electric flux through the small elements \\(\\Delta A_1\\) is\n\\(\\Phi_1=\\vec E_1\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_1=E_1\\Delta A_1\\cos0=E_1\\Delta A_1\\)\nThe electric flux through the other small element \\(\\Delta A_2\\) is\n\\(\\Phi_2=\\vec E_2\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_2=E_2\\Delta A_2\\cos0=E_2\\Delta A_2\\)\nSimilarly the electric flux through \\(\\Delta A_n\\) is\n\\(\\Phi_n=\\vec E_n\\cdot\\Delta\\vec A_n=E_n\\Delta A_n\\cos0=E_n\\Delta A_n\\)\nThe total flux through the entire surface is\n\\(\\Phi_E=\\Phi_1+\\Phi_2+\\Phi_3+\\Phi_4+\\ldots+\\Phi_n\\)\n\\(\\Phi_E=\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}E\\Delta A\\) ...(11.12)\nBut as electric field intensity E is constant over the surface of sphere\nTherefore,\n\\(\\Phi_E=E\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A\\)\nSince,\n\\(E=\\frac{q}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{1}{r^2}\\)\nThus the above equation can be written as\n\\(\\Phi_E=\\frac{q}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{1}{r^2}\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A\\)\n\\(\\sum_{\\mathrm{surface}}\\Delta A=\\) total area enclosed by spherical surface \\(=4\\pi r^2\\)",
