    "title": "TIP — Gaussian-surface flux",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>TIP</p><p>The electric flux through arbitrary Gaussian surface can be calculated as</p><p>\\(\\Phi_E=\\frac{-4\\mu\\mathrm C+2\\mu\\mathrm C+5\\mu\\mathrm C}{\\varepsilon_0}=\\frac{3\\times10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm C}{8.85\\times10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{C^2\\,N^{-1}\\,m^{-2}}}\\)</p><p>\\(=3.4\\times10^5\\,\\mathrm{N\\,m^2\\,C^{-1}}\\)</p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 335 260\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gaussian surface encloses minus4 plus2 plus5 microcoulombs; plus3 and minus4 outside excluded\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:335px\"><path d=\"M100 40Q178 2 219 54T194 161L157 237Q115 242 86 183T100 40Z\" fill=\"#fef08a\"/><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"69\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e11d48\"/><text x=\"121\" y=\"74\" fill=\"#fff\">−</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"74\">−4 μC</text><circle cx=\"171\" cy=\"115\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/><text x=\"166\" y=\"120\" fill=\"#fff\">+</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"120\">+2 μC</text><circle cx=\"126\" cy=\"170\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/><text x=\"121\" y=\"175\" fill=\"#fff\">+</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"175\">+5 μC</text><circle cx=\"253\" cy=\"40\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#0284c7\"/><text x=\"248\" y=\"45\" fill=\"#fff\">+</text><text x=\"267\" y=\"45\">+3 μC</text><circle cx=\"40\" cy=\"218\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e11d48\"/><text x=\"35\" y=\"223\" fill=\"#fff\">−</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"223\">−4 μC</text></svg></figure>",
