    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>In order to give concept of electric potential at a point in an electric field a reference point is required where electric potential is zero and this point is taken at infinity. If point B is at infinity where electric potential is \\(V_B=0\\), while at point A electric potential is \\(V_A=W_{\\infty A}/q_0\\).</p><p>On dropping the subscripts \\(V=\\frac W{q_0}\\)</p><p>Thus the electric potential at any point is equal to the work done in bringing a unit positive charge from infinity to that point without producing any acceleration.</p>",
