    "id": "phys12-front-point30",
    "title": "Point-charge potential — incremental work",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>Now putting the value of E in Eq (11.22) we have</p><p>\\(\\Delta W=\\frac1{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{Qq}{r^2}\\Delta r\\)</p><p>Let the test charge is at a large distance \\(r_A\\) from charge Q. Electric field does not remain constant but varies as the square of the distance from the charge.</p><p>We divide the distance between \\(r_A\\) and \\(r_B\\) into infinitesimally small displacement so that the field intensity over each displacement remains constant.</p><p>Work done between point \\(r_A\\) and \\(r_1\\) is</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_1}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac{r_A-r_1}{r_Ar_1}\\right)\\)</p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 680 320\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Positive source Q, radial field, test charge q at A moved inward, points A/B, rA/rB and intermediate radii rn r3 r2 r1, infinity and delta r\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:680px\"><path d=\"M90 215L170.0 215.0\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M170.0 215.0L163.0 218.0L163.0 212.0Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L146.5685424949238 271.5685424949238\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M146.5685424949238 271.5685424949238L139.49747468305833 268.74011537017765L143.7401153701776 264.49747468305833Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L90.0 295.0\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M90.0 295.0L87.0 288.0L93.0 288.0Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L33.4314575050762 271.5685424949238\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M33.4314575050762 271.5685424949238L36.25988462982239 264.49747468305833L40.50252531694168 268.74011537017765Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L10.0 215.0\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M10.0 215.0L17.0 212.0L17.0 218.0Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L33.43145750507618 158.4314575050762\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M33.43145750507618 158.4314575050762L40.50252531694166 161.2598846298224L36.259884629822366 165.50252531694167Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L89.99999999999999 135.0\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M89.99999999999999 135.0L92.99999999999999 142.0L86.99999999999999 142.0Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215L146.5685424949238 158.4314575050762\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M146.5685424949238 158.4314575050762L143.7401153701776 165.50252531694167L139.49747468305833 161.2598846298224Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M90 215H620\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M620 215L613.0 218.0L613.0 212.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"215\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"84\" y=\"220\">+</text><text x=\"30\" y=\"196\">+Q</text><path d=\"M120 30H245 M245 30V55\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M120 30L127.0 27.0L127.0 33.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M245 30L238.0 33.0L238.0 27.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"248\" y=\"25\">rₙ</text><path d=\"M120 65H340 M340 65V90\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M120 65L127.0 62.0L127.0 68.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M340 65L333.0 68.0L333.0 62.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"343\" y=\"60\">r₃</text><path d=\"M120 100H390 M390 100V125\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M120 100L127.0 97.0L127.0 103.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M390 100L383.0 103.0L383.0 97.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"393\" y=\"95\">r₂</text><path d=\"M120 135H455 M455 135V160\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M120 135L127.0 132.0L127.0 138.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M455 135L448.0 138.0L448.0 132.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"458\" y=\"130\">r₁</text><path d=\"M120 170H530 M530 170V195\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M120 170L127.0 167.0L127.0 173.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M530 170L523.0 173.0L523.0 167.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"533\" y=\"165\">r<tspan baseline-shift=\"sub\" font-size=\"11\">A</tspan></text><path d=\"M90 234H215\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M215 234L208.0 237.0L208.0 231.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><circle cx=\"215\" cy=\"215\" r=\"3\"/><path d=\"M215 215V234\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"204\" y=\"197\">B</text><text x=\"205\" y=\"252\">r<tspan baseline-shift=\"sub\" font-size=\"11\">B</tspan></text><circle cx=\"530\" cy=\"215\" r=\"4\"/><text x=\"516\" y=\"195\">A</text><text x=\"540\" y=\"236\">q</text><text x=\"627\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"32\">∞</text><path d=\"M590 250H534\" stroke=\"#b91c1c\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M534 250L541.0 247.0L541.0 253.0Z\" fill=\"#b91c1c\"/><path d=\"M473 236H530\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"2 4\"/><path d=\"M473 236L480.0 233.0L480.0 239.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M530 236L523.0 239.0L523.0 233.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"473\" y=\"261\">Δr</text></svg><figcaption>FIGURE 11.20: Work done on a test charge q in moving it towards source charge +Q</figcaption></figure>",
    "theory": "Now putting the value of E in Eq (11.22) we have\n\\(\\Delta W=\\frac1{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\frac{Qq}{r^2}\\Delta r\\)\nLet the test charge is at a large distance \\(r_A\\) from charge Q. Electric field does not remain constant but varies as the square of the distance from the charge.\nWe divide the distance between \\(r_A\\) and \\(r_B\\) into infinitesimally small displacement so that the field intensity over each displacement remains constant.\nWork done between point \\(r_A\\) and \\(r_1\\) is\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_1}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac{r_A-r_1}{r_Ar_1}\\right)\\)",
