    "id": "phys12-front-point31",
    "title": "Point-charge potential — summed work and energy",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>By division</p><p>\\(\\therefore\\left(\\frac{r_A}{r_Ar_1}-\\frac{r_1}{r_Ar_1}\\right)=\\left(\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\)</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_1}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\) ...(11.23)</p><p>Similarly for second small displacement \\(\\Delta r=r_1-r_2\\). Work done is</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_1\\to r_2}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_2}-\\frac1{r_1}\\right)\\)</p><p>And</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_n\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1{r_n}\\right)\\) ...(11.24)</p><p>The total work done in moving a charge q from \\(r_A\\) to \\(r_B\\) can be calculated by taking its sum.</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(-\\frac1{r_A}+\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_1}+\\frac1{r_2}-\\frac1{r_2}+\\ldots+\\frac1{r_B}\\right)\\)</p><p>\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\) ...(11.25)</p><p>The work done to move a test charge q from infinity to a distance r from Q is</p><p>\\(W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1\\infty\\right)\\)</p><p>\\(W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}\\right)\\) ...(11.26)</p><p>The electric potential energy at distance r from Q is</p><p>\\(U=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1r\\right)\\) ...(11.27)</p>",
    "theory": "By division\n\\(\\therefore\\left(\\frac{r_A}{r_Ar_1}-\\frac{r_1}{r_Ar_1}\\right)=\\left(\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\)\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_1}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\) ...(11.23)\nSimilarly for second small displacement \\(\\Delta r=r_1-r_2\\). Work done is\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_1\\to r_2}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_2}-\\frac1{r_1}\\right)\\)\nAnd\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_n\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1{r_n}\\right)\\) ...(11.24)\nThe total work done in moving a charge q from \\(r_A\\) to \\(r_B\\) can be calculated by taking its sum.\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(-\\frac1{r_A}+\\frac1{r_1}-\\frac1{r_1}+\\frac1{r_2}-\\frac1{r_2}+\\ldots+\\frac1{r_B}\\right)\\)\n\\(\\Delta W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1{r_A}\\right)\\) ...(11.25)\nThe work done to move a test charge q from infinity to a distance r from Q is\n\\(W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}-\\frac1\\infty\\right)\\)\n\\(W_{r_A\\to r_B}=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1{r_B}\\right)\\) ...(11.26)\nThe electric potential energy at distance r from Q is\n\\(U=\\frac{Qq}{4\\pi\\varepsilon_o}\\left(\\frac1r\\right)\\) ...(11.27)",
