    "id": "phys12-front-dipole39",
    "title": "ELECTRIC DIPOLE",
    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>ELECTRIC DIPOLE</p><p>We know that dielectric materials are made up of the two types of molecules; polar and non polar molecules. A polar molecule like water behaves as a permanent dipole; although electrically neutral as a whole.</p><p>On the other hand, a non-polar molecule like nitrogen has no electric dipole moment in the absence of an external field. In the presence of electric field negative charges in non-polar substance displaces to the opposite of electric field E as shown in Fig11.26. Dipole moments occur when there is a separation of charge. Under the action of external field the centres of negative and positive charges shift and form dipoles. The dipole moment is a measure of the polarity of the molecule.</p><p>The system in which two charges of equal magnitude but of opposite sign separated by the distance d, are present is termed as a dipole. Electric dipole moment is represented by P, which is equal to the product of the charge Q present in the dipole and the distance d between the two charges of the dipole.</p><p>\\(P=|Qd|\\) ...(11.36)</p><p>Where P is a vector quantity.</p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 430 300\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Permanent and induced dipole molecules between charged plates, separation d\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:430px\"><rect x=\"20\" y=\"25\" width=\"28\" height=\"250\" fill=\"#ec4899\"/><rect x=\"326\" y=\"25\" width=\"28\" height=\"250\" fill=\"#38bdf8\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"40\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"40\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"60\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"60\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"80\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"80\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"100\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"100\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"120\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"120\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"140\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"140\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"160\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"160\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"180\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"180\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"200\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"200\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"220\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"220\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"240\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"240\">−</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"260\">+</text><text x=\"332\" y=\"260\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"60\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"60\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"60\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"60\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"55\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"60\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"60\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"83\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"88\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"88\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"83\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"88\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"88\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"83\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"88\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"88\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"111\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"116\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"116\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"111\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"116\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"116\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"111\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"116\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"116\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"139\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"144\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"144\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"139\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"144\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"144\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"139\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"144\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"144\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"167\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"172\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"172\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"167\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"172\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"172\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"167\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"172\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"172\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"200\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"200\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"200\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"200\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"195\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"200\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"200\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"223\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"228\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"228\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"223\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"228\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"228\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"223\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"228\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"228\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"110\" cy=\"251\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"97\" y=\"256\">+</text><text x=\"116\" y=\"256\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"251\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"172\" y=\"256\">+</text><text x=\"191\" y=\"256\">−</text><ellipse cx=\"260\" cy=\"251\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"10\" fill=\"#f9a8d4\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"247\" y=\"256\">+</text><text x=\"266\" y=\"256\">−</text><path d=\"M203 47V243\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/><path d=\"M203 243L200.0 236.0L206.0 236.0Z\" fill=\"#334155\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"147\">d</text><text x=\"373\" y=\"82\">FIGURE 11.26</text></svg><figcaption>FIGURE 11.26</figcaption></figure>",
    "theory": "ELECTRIC DIPOLE\nWe know that dielectric materials are made up of the two types of molecules; polar and non polar molecules. A polar molecule like water behaves as a permanent dipole; although electrically neutral as a whole.\nOn the other hand, a non-polar molecule like nitrogen has no electric dipole moment in the absence of an external field. In the presence of electric field negative charges in non-polar substance displaces to the opposite of electric field E as shown in Fig11.26. Dipole moments occur when there is a separation of charge. Under the action of external field the centres of negative and positive charges shift and form dipoles. The dipole moment is a measure of the polarity of the molecule.\nThe system in which two charges of equal magnitude but of opposite sign separated by the distance d, are present is termed as a dipole. Electric dipole moment is represented by P, which is equal to the product of the charge Q present in the dipole and the distance d between the two charges of the dipole.\n\\(P=|Qd|\\) ...(11.36)\nWhere P is a vector quantity.",
