    "kind": "lesson",
    "content": "<p>Figure shows a different combination of capacitors, if the total charge is 600μC. Then determine the values of V1, and C2.</p><p>GIVEN</p><p>total charge \\(Q=600\\mu\\mathrm C\\), capacitance \\(C_1=15\\mu\\mathrm F\\), capacitance \\(C_3=8\\mu\\mathrm F\\), potential \\(V_2=20\\mathrm V\\)</p><p>REQUIRED</p><p>capacitance \\(C_2=?\\), Potential \\(V_1=?\\)</p><p>SOLUTION</p><p>P.D. across capacitor \\(C_1\\): \\(V_1=\\frac Q{C_1}=\\frac{600\\times10^{-6}}{15\\times10^{-6}}=40\\mathrm V\\)</p><p>Total P.D.: \\(V=V_1+V_2=40+20=60\\mathrm V\\)</p><p>Charge on capacitor \\(C_3\\) is: \\(Q_3=C_3\\times V_2\\)</p><p>\\(=(8\\times10^{-6})\\times20\\)</p><p>\\(=160\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm C=160\\mu\\mathrm C\\)</p><p>Charge on capacitor \\(C_2\\) is: \\(Q_2=600-160=440\\mu\\mathrm C\\)</p><p>Capacitance of capacitor \\(C_2=\\frac{440\\times10^{-6}}{20}=22\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm F=22\\mu\\mathrm F\\)</p><figure><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 410 265\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"C1 in series with parallel C2 and C3; voltage V1 across C1 and V2 across parallel branch\" style=\"width:100%;max-width:410px\"><path d=\"M30 60H380V220H30Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M30 60H100M164 60H210M290 60H380\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><path d=\"M100 42V78M112 42V78M210 42V78M222 42V78\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"2\"/><rect x=\"263\" y=\"34\" width=\"8\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><rect x=\"279\" y=\"34\" width=\"8\" height=\"28\" fill=\"#fef3c7\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M30 220H164M222 220H380\" stroke=\"#334155\"/><path d=\"M164 204V236M184 210V230\" stroke=\"#334155\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"90\" y=\"33\">C₁</text><text x=\"204\" y=\"33\">C₂</text><text x=\"258\" y=\"28\">C₃</text><text x=\"35\" y=\"200\">V₁</text><text x=\"292\" y=\"200\">V₂</text><text x=\"345\" y=\"200\">20V</text><text x=\"193\" y=\"252\">V</text><text x=\"140\" y=\"100\">+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"100\">−</text></svg><figcaption>FIGURE — capacitor combination</figcaption></figure>",
    "theory": "Figure shows a different combination of capacitors, if the total charge is 600μC. Then determine the values of V1, and C2.\nGIVEN\ntotal charge \\(Q=600\\mu\\mathrm C\\), capacitance \\(C_1=15\\mu\\mathrm F\\), capacitance \\(C_3=8\\mu\\mathrm F\\), potential \\(V_2=20\\mathrm V\\)\nREQUIRED\ncapacitance \\(C_2=?\\), Potential \\(V_1=?\\)\nSOLUTION\nP.D. across capacitor \\(C_1\\): \\(V_1=\\frac Q{C_1}=\\frac{600\\times10^{-6}}{15\\times10^{-6}}=40\\mathrm V\\)\nTotal P.D.: \\(V=V_1+V_2=40+20=60\\mathrm V\\)\nCharge on capacitor \\(C_3\\) is: \\(Q_3=C_3\\times V_2\\)\n\\(=(8\\times10^{-6})\\times20\\)\n\\(=160\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm C=160\\mu\\mathrm C\\)\nCharge on capacitor \\(C_2\\) is: \\(Q_2=600-160=440\\mu\\mathrm C\\)\nCapacitance of capacitor \\(C_2=\\frac{440\\times10^{-6}}{20}=22\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm F=22\\mu\\mathrm F\\)",
