      "definition": "This law refers to e.m.f and voltage drops in a closed circuit or closed loop and may be stated as under: In any closed electrical circuit, the algebraic sum of all the electromotive force (e.m.f) and voltage drops in resistor is equal to zero i.e. Algebraic sum of emf + algebraic sum of voltage drops = 0.",
