      "title": "Example 14.3 — motional e.m.f., current and power",
      "question": "EXAMPLE 14.3 — A loop of resistance 0.1 Ω is placed in a magnetic field of 2 T. A conductor of length 0.2 m slides along a loop at velocity 0.2 m s⁻¹. Find (a) the e.m.f. produced if the conductor’s motion is perpendicular to the field, (b) the current through the loop, (c) the electrical power generated, and (d) the input mechanical power.",
      "solution": "SOLUTION (a) — Motional e.m.f. ε = vBℓ = 0.2 × 2 × 0.2 = 0.08 V. (b) Current through the loop is I = ε/R = 0.08 V/0.1 Ω = 0.8 A. (c) Electrical power generated is P₁ = IV = 0.8 A × 0.08 V = 0.064 W. The magnetic force on the current-carrying loop of length ℓ is F = B I ℓ = 2 T × 0.8 A × 0.2 m = 0.32 N. (d) The power needed to move the loop against magnetic force F is P₂ = Fv = 0.32 N × 0.2 m s⁻¹ = 0.064 W.",
