      "id": "phys14-exercise-mcq-1-14-conceptual-1-8",
      "exercise": "Unit 14 exercise",
      "title": "Multiple-choice questions 1–14 and conceptual questions 1–8",
      "questions": "UNIT 14 EXERCISE — MULTIPLE-CHOICE QUESTIONS (choose the best possible answer). 1. For inducing e.m.f. in a coil the basic requirement is: (A) flux should link the coil; (B) change in flux should link the coil; (C) coil should form a closed loop; (D) both (B) and (C) are true. 2. A single-turn coil rotates in a uniform magnetic field at uniform speed; induced e.m.f. is: (A) alternating; (B) steady; (C) pulsating; (D) zero. 3. Dynamically induced e.m.f. is used in: (A) choke; (B) transformer; (C) generator; (D) thermocouple. 4. In Fleming’s left-hand rule the thumb represents: (A) current flow; (B) induced e.m.f.; (C) magnetic field; (D) mechanical force. 5. The field at any point on the axis of a current-carrying coil is: (A) perpendicular to the axis; (B) parallel to the axis; (C) at 45° to the axis; (D) zero. 6. When a coil rotates in a magnetic field, the induced current: (A) continuously changes; (B) remains the same; (C) becomes zero; (D) becomes maximum. 7. In an A.C. generator, increasing the number of turns in the coil: (A) decreases e.m.f.; (B) leaves e.m.f. the same; (C) increases e.m.f.; (D) makes e.m.f. zero. 8. A device in which induced e.m.f. is statically induced is: (A) transformer; (B) A.C. generator; (C) alternator; (D) dynamo. 9. Find mutual-inductance coefficient when magnetic flux changes by 2×10⁻² Wb and current changes by 0.01 A: (A) 2 H; (B) 3 H; (C) 1/2 H; (D) zero. 10. Induced e.m.f. in a coil is proportional to: (A) magnetic flux through the coil; (B) rate of change of magnetic flux through the coil; (C) coil area; (D) product of flux and area. 11. In a coil current changes from 2 to 4 A in 0.05 s. If average induced e.m.f. is 8 V, self-inductance is: (A) 0.2 H; (B) 0.1 H; (C) 0.8 H; (D) 0.04 H. 12. Which quantity remains constant in a step-up transformer? (A) current; (B) voltage; (C) power; (D) heat. 13. A step-up transformer has transformation ratio 3:2. What is secondary voltage if primary voltage is 30 V? (A) 45 V; (B) 15 V; (C) 90 V; (D) 300 V. 14. Eddy current is produced when: (A) a metal is kept in a varying magnetic field; (B) a metal is kept in a steady magnetic field; (C) a circular coil is placed in a steady magnetic field; (D) current is passed through a circular coil.\n\nCONCEPTUAL QUESTIONS — 1. What factors limit the size of the back e.m.f.? 2. Why does back e.m.f. tend to decrease as the rate of doing work increases? 3. In Faraday’s experiments, what is the advantage of using coils with many turns? 4. Show that ε = −ΔΦ/Δt is dimensionally correct. 5. Give the formulae for flux linkage in terms of angular orientation. 6. How does an electromagnetic brake work? 7. How can eddy currents be minimized in a transformer? 8. How is electromagnetic induction used in cooktops in electric ranges?",
