      "title": "Example 15.7 — series R–L–C circuit",
      "question": "EXAMPLE 15.7 — A 220 V, 50 Hz A.C. supply is applied to a coil of inductance 0.06 H and resistance 2.5 Ω in series with a 6.8 μF capacitor. Find impedance, current, phase angle, power factor and power. GIVEN: L=0.06 H; R=2.5 Ω; V=220 V; f=50 Hz; C=6.8 μF. SOLUTION: X_L=2πfL=18.85 Ω; X_C=1/(2πfC)=468 Ω. Z=√[R²+(X_L−X_C)²]=449.2 Ω. I=V/Z=0.4897 A. tanφ=(X_L−X_C)/R=−179.66, so φ=−89.7° and current leads voltage. Power factor cosφ=R/Z=0.00557. P=VI cosφ=220×0.4897×0.00557=0.60007 W.",
