    {
      "id": "textbook-example-7",
      "num": "11.7",
      "title": "Example 11.7",
      "problem": "Figure shows a different combination of capacitors, if the total charge is 600μC. Then determine the values of V1, and C2.",
      "given": [
        "total charge \\(Q=600\\mu\\mathrm C\\), capacitance \\(C_1=15\\mu\\mathrm F\\), capacitance \\(C_3=8\\mu\\mathrm F\\), potential \\(V_2=20\\mathrm V\\)"
      ],
      "required": [
        "capacitance \\(C_2=?\\), Potential \\(V_1=?\\)"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "P.D. across capacitor \\(C_1\\): \\(V_1=\\frac Q{C_1}=\\frac{600\\times10^{-6}}{15\\times10^{-6}}=40\\mathrm V\\)",
        "Total P.D.: \\(V=V_1+V_2=40+20=60\\mathrm V\\)",
        "Charge on capacitor \\(C_3\\) is: \\(Q_3=C_3\\times V_2\\)",
        "\\(=(8\\times10^{-6})\\times20\\)",
        "\\(=160\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm C=160\\mu\\mathrm C\\)",
        "Charge on capacitor \\(C_2\\) is: \\(Q_2=600-160=440\\mu\\mathrm C\\)",
        "Capacitance of capacitor \\(C_2=\\frac{440\\times10^{-6}}{20}=22\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm F=22\\mu\\mathrm F\\)"
      ],
      "answer": "Capacitance of capacitor \\(C_2=\\frac{440\\times10^{-6}}{20}=22\\times10^{-6}\\mathrm F=22\\mu\\mathrm F\\)",
      "solutionOrigin": "textbook",
      "sourceReferences": [
        {
          "pdfPage": 25,
          "printedPage": 40
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "textbook-example-8",
      "num": "11.8",
      "title": "Example 11.8",
      "problem": "A 6μF capacitor is charged to a P.D. of 200V and then connected in parallel with an un-charged 3μF capacitor. Calculate the P.D. across the parallel plate capacitors.",
      "given": [
        "Capacitance of charged capacitor \\(C_1=6\\mu\\mathrm F\\), Capacitance of un-charged capacitor \\(C_2=3\\mathrm{pF}\\), P.D. of capacitor \\(C_1\\) is: \\(V=200\\mathrm V\\)"
      ],
      "required": [
        "P.D. across the parallel plate capacitors \\(V=?\\)"
      ],
      "steps": [
        "Charge on capacitor \\(C_1\\) is: \\(Q=C_1V=(6\\times10^{-6})\\times200=0.0012\\mathrm C\\)",
        "The equivalent capacitance of parallel combination of capacitors is",
        "\\(C_{eq}=C_1+C_2=6+3=9\\mu\\mathrm F\\)",
        "The charge 0.0012 C is distributed between the two capacitors to have a common P.D.",
        "P.D. across parallel plate capacitors: \\(V=\\frac Q{C_T}=\\frac{0.0012}{9\\times10^{-6}}=133.3\\mathrm V\\)"
      ],
      "answer": "P.D. across parallel plate capacitors: \\(V=\\frac Q{C_T}=\\frac{0.0012}{9\\times10^{-6}}=133.3\\mathrm V\\)",
      "solutionOrigin": "textbook",
      "sourceReferences": [
        {
          "pdfPage": 25,
          "printedPage": 40
        }
      ]
    }
